\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar retreats as Fed signals rate-hike cycle nearing its end\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2023\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 11 (Reuters) - The dollar weakened on Tuesday after \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials signalled that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nearing the end of its tightening cycle, although it traded in a tight range ahead of a key U.S. inflation report.\par \par \uc2 Several Fed officials said on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely need to raise interest rates further to bring down inflation but the end to its current monetary policy tightening cycle is getting close.\par \par \uc2 The comments knocked the greenback to a two-month low of 101.71 against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia trade, as traders pared back their expectations about how much further U.S. rates may have to rise.\par \par \uc2 U.S. interest rate expectations have been a key driver of the dollar since the Fed began its tightening cycle last year.\par \par \uc2 Sterling hit a 15-month high of $1.28875, while the euro climbed to a two-month peak of $1.1022.\par \par \uc2 "The FOMC speak was the main focus of yesterday and officials who spoke reiterated the recent message that a couple more rate hikes are likely in coming months, so not really a surprise there," said Carol Kong, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Markets are now focusing their attention on U.S. inflation data due out on Wednesday, which will provide more clarity on the progress the Fed has made in its fight against stubbornly high consumer prices.\par \par \uc2 A survey from the New York Federal Reserve on Monday showed waning near-term inflation expectations among Americans, who said last month they were expecting the weakest near-term inflation gains in just over two years.\par \par \uc2 "If we do get a strong CPI report (tomorrow), that may help market pricing for a second rate hike from the FOMC (after July) and drive the dollar a little bit higher," said Kong. "But I don't think any upside will be material given the fact that we are near the top of the FOMC tightening cycle."\par \par \uc2 In Asia, the yen was among the biggest gainers, strengthening past 141 per dollar for the first time in nearly a month and last trading at 140.77.\par \par \uc2 The yen has risen roughly 3% from a seven-month low touched last month, when it weakened past the closely watched 145 per dollar level that put traders on high alert for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities.\par \par \uc2 "(The yen) started to stall earlier on, close to 145, and that's because there were concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Moh Siong Sim.\par \par \uc2 He said rising Japanese government bond yields, alongside a weaker dollar, have also contributed to the stronger yen.\par \par \uc2 "The market is starting to wake up again to the idea that there is a (\uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 ) policy risk going into the July meeting... Given the rising inflation backdrop in Japan, the market is starting to become more wary that perhaps a policy tweak could come."\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Australian dollar rose 0.14% to $0.6686, while the New Zealand dollar steadied at $0.6210.\par \par \uc2 The offshore Chinese yuan edged higher, last trading at 7.2048 per dollar, with sentiment underpinned by an extension of financial policy support from \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the country's beleaguered property sector.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rae Wee; Editing by Shri Navaratnam and Edmund Klamann) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-11T07:04:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230711ej7b00ilp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
