\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen steady, markets on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  alert; Aussie up before \uc2 RBA\uc2  decision\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2023\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ankur Banerjee\par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 4 (Reuters) - The yen nudged up on\par Tuesday but remained vulnerable to more  weakness, hovering near\par the key 145 per dollar level as markets were on alert for signs\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while the Australian dollar moved up ahead of a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy decision. \par     The yen was up 0.17% at 144.42 per dollar in early\par Asian hours, but remained close to last week's eight month low\par of 145.07 per dollar that prompted Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi\par Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  to warn against excessive yen selling.\par      Earlier on Tuesday, Japan's top financial diplomat Masato\par Kanda said that officials were in close contact with \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other overseas authorities\par almost everyday on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and broader financial markets.\par     "This is sending signals that a coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par be coming as yen continues to hover above 144 per dollar," said\par Charu Chanana, market strategist at Saxo Markets. \par     "A coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually has a longer lasting\par impact on the yen than a unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have." \par     Japan bought yen in September, its first foray in the market\par to boost its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since 1998, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pledge\par to retain ultra-loose policy as long as required drove the yen\par as low as 145 per dollar. It \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in October after\par the yen plunged to a 32-year low of 151.94.\par     Against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar eased\par 0.039% to 102.910 after data overnight showed U.S. manufacturing\par slumped further in June, reaching levels last seen when the\par nation was reeling from the initial wave of the COVID-19\par pandemic.\par      "We expect the U.S. economy to face a recession starting in\par Q3 23," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kristina Clifton\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adding that it was likely to be\par a quiet day for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market with no major data releases\par or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speech scheduled. U.S. markets are closed for\par the July 4 Independence Day holiday. \par     Investor focus this week will be on nonfarm payrolls data\par along with jobs report for more clues about the broader labour\par market in the United States. Minutes of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's June meeting are also due to be released on Wednesday.\par     Markets are pricing in a near 87% chance of a 25 basis point\par hike in the next Federal Reserve meeting at the end of the\par month, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME\f28 \uc2 \f2  FedWatch tool showed. \par     \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2  WATCH\par     The focus in Asian hours will be on the policy decision from\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ). \par     Markets are leaning towards a pause, with swaps pricing a\par 63% chance of a hold in rates after data last week showed\par consumer inflation slowed to a 13-month low in May. But\par economists were split on the outcome, with 16 out of 31 polled\par by Reuters expecting a hike and the rest forecasting the bank to\par stand pat. \par     Since a surprise pause in April and subsequent hikes in May\par and June, economists have been mostly divided in recent months\par over the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2 's next move.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 CBA\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Clifton said the slight easing in inflation in May\par should please the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2  but with a tight labour market as well as\par still high price pressures, a 25 bps hike would not be a\par surprise. \par     "We estimate that a hike would push up Aussie modestly by\par 0.8% so long as the post-meeting statement was not dovish.  No\par change or a dovish hike could pull AUD modestly lower." \par     The Australian dollar <AUD-D3> was at $0.668, up 0.16%\par against the U.S. dollar, while the New Zealand dollar\par was also up 0.16% at $0.616.\par     The euro was up 0.02% to $1.0913, while sterling\par  was last at $1.2699, up 0.06% on the day.  \par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0209 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0908        $1.0915     -0.04%         +1.82%      +1.0915     +1.0908\par  Dollar/Yen                   144.6100   