\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar flat; Aussie slides as inflation slows\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 28 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar was barely changed on Wednesday, with resilient economic data easing investor worries over a recession and lifting risk sentiment, though that also indicated that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  may have to continue raising rates.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar fell sharply as consumer inflation eased in May.\par \par \uc2 Data showed that U.S. consumer confidence increased in June to the highest level in nearly 1-1/2 years, while business spending appeared to hold up in May, indicating the economy remained on solid footing.\par \par \uc2 Markets are pricing in a 77% probability of a 25 basis point hike by the Fed next month, according to \uc2 CME\uc2  FedWatch tool, but no more after that.\par \par \uc2 Against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar rose 0.029% to 102.53, after slipping 0.24% overnight. The dollar index is on course to log a decline of about 1.5% for the month.\par \par \uc2 Rodrigo Catril\uc2 , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 , said US data is feeding the theme of 'sectoral recessions' playing with different lags, making the Fed's job to tame inflation harder.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, the data is telling us the Fed needs to keep its foot on the tightening pedal."\par \par \uc2 Investor attention will firmly be on Fed Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's comments at the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Forum in Sintra, Portugal, which could provide cues on the path of interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "We expect Powell to reaffirm his hawkish policy stance," said Carol Kong, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 . "Though we doubt his comments will materially push up FOMC pricing."\par \par \uc2 Powell will be in a panel along with \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's Andrew Bailey, \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's Kazuo Ueda.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Australian dollar fell 0.72% to $0.6637 after the Australian consumer price inflation rate slowed to a 13-month low in May, driven by a sharp pullback in fuel.\par \par \uc2 A measure of core inflation also cooled, in a sign interest rates might not have to rise again in July.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was 0.47% lower against the dollar at $0.613.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro was down 0.1% at $1.0948, after rising 0.5% overnight following hawkish comments from \uc2 ECB\uc2  President Lagarde. Sterling was at $1.2734, down 0.09% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen strengthened 0.16% to 143.81 per dollar, but remained close to the seven-month low of 144.18 it touched on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities are under renewed pressure to combat the yen's fresh declines driven by market expectations that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will keep interest rates ultra-low, even as other central banks tighten monetary policy to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 "With the rise in the dollar against the yen set to run further, we judge the risk has increased the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying the JPY," \uc2 CBA\uc2 's Kong said.\par \par \uc2 "However, we note it is the speed of change, rather than the level, that matters most in the MoF\u8217\'20\'19s decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; Editing by Muralikumar Anantharaman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-28T03:23:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230628ej6s0070t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
