\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar fends off another suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  from Japan\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2022\par 07:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 24 (Reuters) - Suspected Bank of Japan (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave only brief respite to the Japanese yen as the dollar stayed strong on Monday, while sterling wavered as former finance minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  emerged as frontrunner to become Britain's prime minister.\par \par \uc2 The yen hit a low of 149.70 per dollar in early deals before being swept to a high of 145.28 within minutes in a move that suggested the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , acting for \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), had stepped in for a second successive day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, dropped back to near 148.88.\par \par \uc2 "The price action should be worrying for the MOF, as it suggests that there is strong demand to buy into dollar/yen dips," said Sean Wallow, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 "The timing should have been good for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with U.S. yields still falling in the wake of the WSJ Fed story Friday."\par \par \uc2 Stocks rallied and U.S. yields fell on Friday after the Wall Street Journal reported \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials will likely debate the size of future hikes, fuelling hopes that a Fed pivot might be near.\par \par \uc2 Japan had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying yen in the second confirmed instance in a month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 32-year low near 152 to the dollar, policy sources said.\par \par \uc2 That triggered a rally of more than 7 yen for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 144.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Damien Boey, chief macro strategist at Sydney-based investment firm Barrenjoey, said the Japanese yen was still not close to fair value.\par \par \uc2 "When I run some of the parity condition and evaluation models for dollar/yen, you get some really crazy results like the fair value could be at 170," said Boey.\par \par \uc2 "This just goes to show how important it is for the U.S. to drive the U.S. dollar back down, because the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , doing what it is doing, is not able to do it."\par \par \uc2 Traders also suspect the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  has stepped in on other occasions in the past month to shore up a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has tumbled 22% this year against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Referring to how Japan had a classic open economy 'trilemma' forcing it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets concurrently, Goldman analysts said: "While sub-optimal and unsustainable in the medium term, we think this policy mix could be in place for some time."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar also made gains against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the dollar index up 0.3% at 112.24.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.2% to $0.9831.\par \par \uc2 Sterling also see-sawed on news former prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  had dropped out of running for British prime minister and was last up 0.2% at $1.1320, trimming earlier agains.\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  said he has withdrawn from Monday's contest to replace \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , who was forced to resign after she launched an economic programme that triggered turmoil on financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Former Chancellor \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  has emerged as the clear frontrunner to become Britain's next prime minister.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar was down 0.7% versus the greenback at $0.6330, while the kiwi also eased 0.3% on its U.S. peer at $0.573.\par \par \uc2 In cryptocurrencies, bitcoin last rose 0.7% to $19,316.00.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Stella Qiu and Wayne Cole in Sydney; Editing by Shri Navaratnam & Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-24T06:10:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221024eiao00nud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
