\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen pulls back from precipice as traders fear  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 06:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Tom Westbrook\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 30 (Reuters) - The battered yen bounced on\par Wednesday as traders began doubting whether Japanese authorities\par would tolerate too much more weakness, while hopes for a\par breakthrough in Russia-Ukraine peace talks helped the euro and\par dragged on the dollar.\par     The yen rose more than 1% to 121.32 per dollar,\par with a meeting between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko\par Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fumio Kishida\f28 \uc2 \f2  adding to speculation\par about the level of official discomfort with a falling yen.\par \par     It has lost more than 5% on the dollar in March.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  is not going to be very happy with unmitigated and\par really abrupt yen weakness," said Vishnu Varathan, chief\par economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Jawboning or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par remains a risk if such excessive moves continue, and I think\par that must have dawned on markets, with the convenient\par coincidence of long-end U.S. yields taking a step back as well,"\par he said.\par     "The fact that (Kuroda and Kishida) are speaking ... shows\par that there is a wider consultation."\par     The yawning gap between a hawkish \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a\par dovish \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  has driven the yen's drop and on Wednesday\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  extended bond purchases along the curve as part of its\par effort to defend a 0.25% 10-year yield target.\par     The whipsaw in the yen this week has lifted overnight\par dollar/yen implied volatility to its highest since the\par U.S. presidential election in November 2020.\par     Elsewhere moves were much smaller, with the euro\par up 0.2% to $1.1111 as it edged back toward an overnight two-week\par high of $1.137. Heavily sold on fears of the economic fallout\par from war in Ukraine and nerves about the risk of the conflict\par spreading west, it has been a beneficiary of hopes for peace.\par     The common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  jumped through its 200-day moving\par average on the pound on Tuesday and held at\par three-month high of 84.82 pence on Wednesday.\par     Russia's rouble sat at 89 to the dollar after\par hitting a month-high of 83.50 in offshore trade on Tuesday.\par     Russia has promised to scale down military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around\par Kyiv and Ukraine proposed adopting a neutral status in a sign of\par progress at face-to-face negotiations in Istanbul.\par     However, U.S. officials have since poured a little bit of\par cold water on hopes for a deal by warning the threat to Kyiv\par isn't over.\par     "At least the two sides are talking," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank\par of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Joe Capurso.\par     "The tentative good news about the war will benefit the euro\par more than any other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  given Europe's proximity to the\par conflict and reliance on Russian energy," he said.\par     The mood also proved helpful for risk-sensitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars. They were firm\par just below recent peaks in morning trade, with the Aussie\par  at $0.7512 and kiwi at $0.6946.\par     The South Korean won, which like the euro has\par been battered by the leap in oil prices since war began just\par over a month ago, jumped 1% to 1,208.5 per dollar.\par     \par ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0405 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.1117        $1.1086     +0.28%         +0.00%      +1.1121     +1.1080\par  Dollar/Yen                   121.7000       122.8950    -0.96%         +0.00%      +123.2000   +121.4500\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  135.29         136.22      -0.68%         +0.00%      +136.6700   +134.8900\par                   S>                                                                            \par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9284         0.9307      -0.23%         +0.00%      +0.9313     +0.9278\par  Sterling/Dollar              1.3106         1.3095      +0.09%         +0.00%      +1.3111     +1.3091\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.2490         1.2503      -0.09%         +0.00%      +1.2508     +1.2490\par  Aussie/Dollar                0.7520         0.7508      +0.17%         +0.00%      +0.7524     +0.7504\par  NZ                           0.6961         0.6935      +0.37%         +0.00%      +0.6964     +0.6933\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                  \par                                                                             