\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken as worries on U.S.-China trade talks rise\b0\par\par\uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2019\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Yuan ends a four-day losing streak\par     * Thai baht strengthens ahead of c.bank meeting \par     * China April exports contract, while imports rise\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     May 8 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Wednesday, as fresh  doubts about whether the United States and\par China can end their trade war rekindled worries about global\par growth.\par     Beijing said on Tuesday that Chinese Vice Premier Liu He\par will travel to Washington for two days of talks starting on\par Thursday, setting up a last-ditch bid for a deal that would\par avoid a sharp increase in tariffs on Chinese goods ordered by\par U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The higher tariffs are scheduled to take effect on Friday,\par when Liu would be in Washington.\par     The South Korean won on Wednesday weakened as\par much as 0.5 percent to 1,172.50 against the dollar. \par     South Korea's finance minister flagged increasing downside\par risks for his country, a further sign of weakness for Asia's\par fourth largest economy following a sharp contraction in first\par quarter growth and sluggish exports.\par     Sim Moh Siong, an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said\par sentiment in Asia is "still one of wariness that if trade\par tensions escalate, there could be a further round of weakness in\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ".  \par     "Markets are trying to make out whether we are likely to see\par a replay of a tale of two halves or is everything going to\par collapse into a situation where it is not quite clear whether\par the U.S. dollar will emerge as the winner if the trade war\par escalates."\par     The Indian rupee weakened 0.3 percent to its lowest\par level in more than a week, while the Indonesian rupiah\par declined 0.2 percent. \par     Data released on Wednesday showed China's exports\par unexpectedly shrank in April but imports surprised with their\par first increase in five months, painting a mixed picture of the\par health of the Chinese economy.\par     However, the yuan snapped four days of losses to\par edge up against the dollar, supported by a rise in corporate\par dollar selling after \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a firmer midpoint.\par \par     The Thai baht, bucking the regional trend,\par strengthened 0.4 percent to its best level in three weeks, ahead\par of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting that is widely expected to keep the\par benchmark rate unchanged for a third straight review.\par \par     The Philippine peso edged lower, ahead of Thursday's\par release of first quarter growth data and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par decision.  \par     With inflation slowing for a sixth consecutive month in\par April, there are growing expectations that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangko Sentral ng\par Pilipinas\f28 \uc2 \f2  will ease monetary policy. \par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par     The Singapore dollar appreciated 0.2 percent against\par the dollar on the day.\par     "The Singapore dollar is a safe haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Southeast\par Asia and so there is definitely some demand due to the\par tremendous uncertainties around U.S.-China trade negotiations,"\par Margaret Yang Yan, a market analyst at CMC Markets said.\par     Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday it would disclose\par more information on the actions it takes to implement monetary\par policy, including releasing data on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  every six months.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manages policy through\par exchange rate settings rather than interest rates. \par     \par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0521 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0521 GMT                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              109.990     110.24        +0.23\par  Sing dlr               1.360       1.3626        +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr             30.912      30.911        -0.00\par  Korean won             1168.900    1166.5        -0.21\par  Baht                   31.770      31.89         +0.38\par  Peso                   52.020      52.01         -0.02\par  Rupiah                 14308.000   14275         -0.23\par  Rupee                  69.605      69.43         -0.26\par  Ringgit                4.146       4.147         +0.02\par  Yuan                   6.771       6.7780        +0.11\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2019                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2018      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              109.990     109.56   