\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit hits lowest since 1998, Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  dented by Fed outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2016\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds text, updates prices)\par     * Ringgit hits lowest vs dollar since January 1998\par     * Singapore dollar hits 7-year low, later turns higher\par     * Won hits 6-1/2 month low; baht hits lowest in nearly 11\par months\par \par     By Masayuki Kitano\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 20 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit slipped\par to its weakest level in nearly 19 years versus the dollar on\par Tuesday as prospects of a faster pace of U.S. interest rate\par rises in 2017 kept the greenback well bid.\par     The ringgit fell to 4.4790  per dollar as of\par 0556 GMT, its weakest level since January 1998, during the Asian\par financial crisis. It last stood at 4.4780, little changed on the\par day.\par     The Singapore dollar hit a seven-year low of 1.4507 per U.S.\par dollar. It later turned higher, however, with market\par participants citing suspected U.S. dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .     \par     The South Korean won and the Thai baht touched multi-month\par lows, as downward pressure on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  persisted after\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised interest rates last week and\par signalled three hikes in 2017, more than it had expected\par earlier.    \par     The won hit a low of 1193.0 per dollar at one\par point, its weakest level since early June. The baht fell to \par 35.911, its lowest level since late January.\par     While financial markets were rattled by deadly incidents in\par Turkey and Germany on Monday, analysts said the impact on\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seemed to be limited. \par     A truck ploughed into a crowded Christmas market in central\par Berlin on Monday evening, killing 12 people and injuring 48\par others while the Russian ambassador to Turkey was shot dead as\par he gave a speech at an Ankara art gallery. \par  \par     The incidents "do not appear to eclipse the optimism over\par the U.S. economy," said Philip Wee, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist\par for DBS Bank, adding that comments from Fed Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday reinforced the positive view on the U.S. economy.\par     In a speech on Monday, Yellen noted that college graduates\par were entering the strongest jobs market in nearly a decade.\par     \par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have declined broadly since early\par November, as the dollar and U.S. bond yields jumped on\par expectations that U.S. President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's proposals\par for infrastructure spending and tax cuts will boost economic\par growth and inflation.\par     The rise in U.S. bond yields has stirred worries about the\par risk of capital outflows from emerging markets, putting downward\par pressure on emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par      \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The rupiah slipped 0.1 percent versus the dollar. \par     An Indonesia-based trader said the rupiah was pressured\par partly by year-end demand for dollars among local firms.\par            \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \par   Change on the day at   0555 GMT                         \par   \f28 