\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Growing US tightening fears rattle Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; yuan hits 8-1/2-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 992 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2016\par 05:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixing weakest since June 2008; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par suspected\par     * Won slumps on bond outflows, foreigners sell Korean\par equities\par     * Ringgit near 14-month low as Malaysia bonds hit\par     * Rupiah around 6-month trough; Singapore dlr at 10-month\par low\par     * Philippine peso hits 2008-global financial crisis level\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par skidded on Thursday as views grew that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will\par tighten more aggressively given solid U.S. economic data, adding\par to pressure from higher Treasury yields and fears over\par Washington's trade protectionism.\par     The Chinese yuan hit an 8-1/2-year low after the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set its daily guidance rate at its\par weakest since June 2008.\par     Chinese state-owned banks sold dollars as the renminbi\par weakened toward the psychological 7 per dollar level, traders\par said.  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities in India, Indonesia and the\par Philippines were also suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday to\par curb losses in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     South Korea's won led regional depreciation on\par bond outflows and as foreign investors were set to reverse a\par buying spree in the equity market.\par     The Malaysian ringgit hit an almost 14-month\par trough, tracking slides in most government bond prices\par .\par     Indonesia's rupiah fell to a near six-month low as\par foreign investors continued to sell local stocks. Most\par long-term government bond prices slid.\par     The Singapore dollar touched a 10-month trough on\par dollar strength and after the city-state downgraded its\par forecasts for economic growth and exports for this year after\par confirmed a third-quarter contraction. \par     The Philippine peso slumped to levels last seen\par in November 2008 as foreign investors keep dumping Manila shares\par .\par     The U.S. dollar hovered around a 14-year peak against\par a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as markets are now pricing in a\par nearly 100 percent probability of a December Fed rate increase,\par according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME\f28 \uc2 \f2  FedWatch.\par     Some investors expect more hikes in 2017 if economic\par momentum is sustained.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields extended their rise. The two-year yield\par  hit its highest levels since April 2010 on Wednesday\par as the market continued to bet that the incoming administration\par of President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  will increase debt-funded\par spending and spur higher growth and inflation.\par     Manufactured capital goods in the world's largest economy\par rebounded last month on rising demand for machinery and\par equipment. Consumer sentiment also rose this month with Trump's\par election viewed as positive for their personal finances and the\par economy. \par     "Strong U.S. macro data, surging inflation expectations\par arising from Trump's pro-growth stance and a more hawkish Fed\par will hurt EM Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  further, although their weakness\par is technically seen excessive," said Qi Gao, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par with Scotiabank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Any corrections in the USD and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will provide\par chances to buy the USD," Gao said, referring to central banks of\par emerging Asia's efforts to support their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have suffered from capital outflows on\par rising U.S. yields and growing concerns that Trump's\par protectionist stance on trade will hit Asian exports.\par     \par     WON\par     The won fell as South Korea posted a combined 878.1 billion\par won ($742.2 million) worth of bond outflows in the first 23 days\par of the month, a preliminary data from a financial regulator\par showed.\par     Foreign investors also sold a net 125.4 billion won worth of\par shares in the local main stock exchange by mid-afternoon to snap\par a five-day buying streak.\par     A deepening political scandal has added to bearish\par sentiment.\par     Investigators raided the offices of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lotte Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par and government agencies earlier in the day, officials said, as\par part of a widening probe into alleged influence-peddling that\par has engulfed President Park Geun-hye. \par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered some of earlier losses\par on expectations of demand from exporters for month-end\par settlements.\par     Caution also grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem its weakness.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit lost 0.5 percent to 4.4630 per dollar, its\par weakest since Sept. 29, 2015, when the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a\par 17-year low.\par     Short-term foreign investors sold the unit, while\par hedging-related dollar bids also hurt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah slumped 0.4 percent to 13,540 per dollar, its\par weakest since June 3.\par     Foreign investors offloaded 7.6 trillion rupiah's ($561.5\par million) worth of Indonesian equities over the previous 11\par straight sessions.\par     Most long-term government bond prices fell with the 10-year\par yield at 8.082 percent, its highest since March 3.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the\par session low, traders said.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  112.71         112.50     -0.19\par   Sing dlr                   1.4339         1.4318     -0.15\par   Taiwan dlr                 31.930         31.880     -0.16\par   Korean won                1183.10        1176.20     -0.58\par   Baht                        35.70          35.57     -0.36\par   Peso                       49.999         49.860     -0.28\par   Rupiah                      13535          13480     -0.41\par   Rupee                       68.83          68.56     -0.39\par   Ringgit                    4.4550         4.4400     -0.34\par   Yuan                       6.9203         6.9190     -0.02\par                                                             \par   Change so far in 2016                  