\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Stocks Underperforms Asia Markets as 1MDB Scandal Drags -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2016\par 03:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 01:50 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The FTSE \uc2 Bursa Malaysia\uc2  Index declines Thursday morning despite positive Asian markets buoyed by overnight gains on Wall Street and recovery in oil prices. Stocks market in the oil exporting country are down on domestic political uncertainty after the \uc2 U.S. Justice Department\uc2  filed lawsuit in attempting to seize around $1 billion in assets related to Malaysia's state fund 1MDB founded by Prime Minister \uc2 Najib Razak\uc2 . The Malaysian 30-stocks benchmark index declines 0.48% to 1,664.66 points in early trade. The top losers are property-to-plantations conglomerate \uc2 PPB Group\uc2  (4065.KU) and gas processing firm \uc2 Petronas Gas\uc2  (6033.KU).\par \par \uc2  The top gainers are ports operator Westports Holdings (5246.KU) and pay TV firm \uc2 Astro Malaysia Holdings\uc2  (6399.KU). (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; @yantoultra)\par \par \uc2 0146 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Asian rice prices have picked up again in 2016 as a result of the dry weather recorded in since 4Q15 and sharp declines in local rice production, says BMI Research in a note. "We believe they will remain supported over the coming months before easing in 2017 thanks to the post-El Ni\u241\'00\'F1o pick up in production next year." It notes that plentiful monsoon rains in India so far and the end of the drought recorded in South East Asia in 1H16 will also lead to bumper crops in 2016/17. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com;Twitter: @lucy_craymer)\par \par \uc2 01:48 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 St. Barbara Ltd\uc2 .'s (SBM.AU) comeback is complete, declares Macquarie. It says higher 4Q16 gold output offered "a strong finish" to what was a "transformational year" for the Australia-listed miner. "We expect the strong performance to continue and note that St. Barbara has the highest free cash-flow yield in our gold coverage universe," it says. Still, after a more-than doubling in the value of its stock year-to-date, Macquarie thinks the miner is fairly valued and keeps a neutral rating. Investors are cashing in on the rally, with St. Barbara recently down 10% at A$2.98/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 01:45 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Shares of Singapore public transport operator SMRT (S53.SG) rise 7.4% to S$1.66, close to \uc2 Temasek Holding\uc2 's offer of S$1.68 (US$1.24) apiece for all the shares the state investor doesn't already own. \uc2 Temasek\uc2  and SMRT announced the open offer Wednesday. SMRT resumed trading Thursday after staying on halt since Friday. \uc2 Temasek\uc2 , which currently owns a 54% of SMRT, plans to take it private to let the operator repair its image following a series of train faults in recent years. However, SMRT shares may not rise further, unless investors dig in and force \uc2 Temasek\uc2  to sweeten the deal. Most analysts predict a weak outlook for the operator after the government announced last week that it would take over its train assets and leave it to focus only on \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 01:06 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The pace of decline in South Korea's exports will likely continue to moderate in July, show latest customs data that may offer a glimmering hope for recovery in demand overseas. Korean shipments for the first 20 days of July fell 1.9% from a year earlier, according to the Korea Customs Service Thursday. The latest customes figure--though a rough guide to trade for the full month--signals a trend of a slower pace of decline in exports. Exports shrank 2.7% on-year in June following a 6% fall in May and an 11.2% drop in April. Korean shipments overseas had been in decline since January in 2015 on sluggish global trade, lower oil prices and a slowdown in China. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 01:00 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/SGD is up for a third day in a row, as the Singapore dollar loses more of its shine while the Japanese yen continues to depreciate. The yen is a key component of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket used by Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value. Last week, the Singapore dollar was at a record high against the basket, prompting calls by analysts to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to halt its relative appreciation. The USD/JPY pair rallied to a 1.5-month high earlier, on a continuation of bets that Japan will soon announce fresh fiscal stimulus. The easing bias of global central banks remains the dominant theme for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some analysts suggest that the MAS could even ease the slope of the Singapore dollar's managed valuation path again--which was flattened in April--implying an engineered depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/SGD is now 1.3585 from its Wednesday closing of 1.3560 (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:52 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Rio Tinto Ltd\uc2 .'s (RIO.AU) stock has overshot, according to \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 . Its Australian shares have rallied 8% year-to-date, aided by better-than-expected iron-ore prices. "We think the market is too bullish on steelmaking materials, aluminum and copper with the transition of China's economy from investment to consumption underestimated," it says. \uc2 Morningstar\uc2  has a fair-value estimate on the stock of A$31/share. It trades up 0.6% at A$48.27/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 0038 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yen is likely to regain if the BOJ policy setters disappoint investors next week (July 28-29), says SMBC Nikko chief rate strategist Chotaro Morita, in a morning note. "How much the yen will bounce back is now discussed among investors," after rising on expectations for Tokyo's strong policy steps, says Morita. If an extra BOJ easing is already factored in to allow the USD/JPY's rise above the 107-line (now at 107.24), the USD/JPY will likely "fall by several yen depending on the BOJ policy decision," says Morita. A falloff straight to below Y100 is unlikely. But whether the BOJ can allow fragility of the USD/JPY potential to decline below Y100 on possible risk events will likely determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy decision, he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:32 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] After reviewing department store chain \uc2 Myer Holdings Ltd\uc2 .'s (MYR.AU) central Brisbane, Australia, store, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  says it has become more positive on the fourth quarter outlook for the stock. The broker says there appeared to be a relatively low level of winter stock in the store, mark-down rates were low and new season products were evident. "There was simple, but effective point of sale emphasising new arrivals," say analysts Grant Saligari and Troy O'Dwyer in a research note, adding they were greeted on entry to the store. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  has an outperform rating and A$1.40/share price target on the stock, above its recent trade at A$1.245. "Recent evidence of a relatively low level of markdown activity and new stock in stores suggests better trading than we had previously expected in 4Q," the analysts say.(rebecca.thurlow@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2027 ET -- \uc2 Crown Holdings\uc2  (CCK), which makes beverage, food and aerosol cans, said it is on track for a "very strong 2016" after exceeding its 2Q earnings view. CCK's adjusted earnings rose to $1.19 from $1.03, compared with a projected range of $1.05 to $1.15. Sales, however, declined to $2.14B from $2.28B, reflecting the pass-through of lower material costs and a $60M \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  effect. CCK has been opening and expanding factories to meet rising demand. Last month, it started commercial production at its Cambodian beverage can plant in Phnom Penh. CCK shares rose 1.2% to $52.89 after hours. (josh.beckerman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:21 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to encounter continued weakness, as the Japanese yen, which has a bearing on several key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, stumbles lower, and the U.S. dollar index touched a new four-month high overnight. The USD/JPY pair has breached the 107.00 round-figure trading barrier, and could be on its way even higher, technical charts suggest. As the yen falls, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are managed by their respective central banks via a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -basket system tend to follow. China's yuan, the Singapore dollar, and the South Korea won to some extent, fall into this category. Others in the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spectrum are likely to follow, as the dominant theme of global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing remains the only game in town for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. Later today, the \uc2 Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may announce another cut in its base interest rate. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last trimmed its key rate by 0.25 percentage point in June. The senior deputy governor has said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on an easing path. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0003 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 MillerCoors\uc2 ' decision to raise its stake in \uc2 Terrapin Beer Co\uc2 . signals that years of moving into craft at turtle-like speed may be coming to an end. After years of its joint-venture owners \uc2 SABMiller\uc2  and Molson debating craft acquisitions, \uc2 MillerCoors\uc2  has now done its second deal in less than a year, taking a majority stake in Athens, Ga.-based Terrapin. With TAP set to take full control over \uc2 MillerCoors\uc2  before the end of the year, will more craft beer deals follow? (tripp.mickle@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 20, 2016 21:50 ET (01:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160721ec7l0004t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
