\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Loses Shine on Tarnished Japanese Yen --\b0\par\par\uc2 1,646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2016\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 01:00 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/SGD is up for a third day in a row, as the Singapore dollar loses more of its shine while the Japanese yen continues to depreciate. The yen is a key component of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket used by Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to monitor its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value. Last week, the Singapore dollar was at a record high against the basket, prompting calls by analysts to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to halt its relative appreciation. The USD/JPY pair rallied to a 1.5-month high earlier, on a continuation of bets that Japan will soon announce fresh fiscal stimulus. The easing bias of global central banks remains the dominant theme for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some analysts suggest that the MAS could even ease the slope of the Singapore dollar's managed valuation path again--which was flattened in April--implying an engineered depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  USD/SGD is now 1.3585 from its Wednesday closing of 1.3560 (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:52 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Rio Tinto Ltd\uc2 .'s (RIO.AU) stock has overshot, according to \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 . Its Australian shares have rallied 8% year-to-date, aided by better-than-expected iron-ore prices. "We think the market is too bullish on steelmaking materials, aluminum and copper with the transition of China's economy from investment to consumption underestimated," it says. \uc2 Morningstar\uc2  has a fair-value estimate on the stock of A$31/share. It trades up 0.6% at A$48.27/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 0038 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yen is likely to regain if the BOJ policy setters disappoint investors next week (July 28-29), says SMBC Nikko chief rate strategist Chotaro Morita, in a morning note. "How much the yen will bounce back is now discussed among investors," after rising on expectations for Tokyo's strong policy steps, says Morita. If an extra BOJ easing is already factored in to allow the USD/JPY's rise above the 107-line (now at 107.24), the USD/JPY will likely "fall by several yen depending on the BOJ policy decision," says Morita. A falloff straight to below Y100 is unlikely. But whether the BOJ can allow fragility of the USD/JPY potential to decline below Y100 on possible risk events will likely determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy decision, he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:32 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] After reviewing department store chain \uc2 Myer Holdings Ltd\uc2 .'s (MYR.AU) central Brisbane, Australia, store, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  says it has become more positive on the fourth quarter outlook for the stock. The broker says there appeared to be a relatively low level of winter stock in the store, mark-down rates were low and new season products were evident. "There was simple, but effective point of sale emphasising new arrivals," say analysts Grant Saligari and Troy O'Dwyer in a research note, adding they were greeted on entry to the store. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  has an outperform rating and A$1.40/share price target on the stock, above its recent trade at A$1.245. "Recent evidence of a relatively low level of markdown activity and new stock in stores suggests better trading than we had previously expected in 4Q," the analysts say.(rebecca.thurlow@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2027 ET -- \uc2 Crown Holdings\uc2  (CCK), which makes beverage, food and aerosol cans, said it is on track for a "very strong 2016" after exceeding its 2Q earnings view. CCK's adjusted earnings rose to $1.19 from $1.03, compared with a projected range of $1.05 to $1.15. Sales, however, declined to $2.14B from $2.28B, reflecting the pass-through of lower material costs and a $60M \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  effect. CCK has been opening and expanding factories to meet rising demand. Last month, it started commercial production at its Cambodian beverage can plant in Phnom Penh. CCK shares rose 1.2% to $52.89 after hours. (josh.beckerman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 00:21 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to encounter continued weakness, as the Japanese yen, which has a bearing on several key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, stumbles lower, and the U.S. dollar index touched a new four-month high overnight. The USD/JPY pair has breached the 107.00 round-figure trading barrier, and could be on its way even higher, technical charts suggest. As the yen falls, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are managed by their respective central banks via a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -basket system tend to follow. China's yuan, the Singapore dollar, and the South Korea won to some extent, fall into this category. Others in the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spectrum are likely to follow, as the dominant theme of global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing remains the only game in town for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. Later today, the \uc2 Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may announce another cut in its base interest rate. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last trimmed its key rate by 0.25 percentage point in June. The senior deputy governor has said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on an easing path. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0003 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 MillerCoors\uc2 ' decision to raise its stake in \uc2 Terrapin Beer Co\uc2 . signals that years of moving into craft at turtle-like speed may be coming to an end. After years of its joint-venture owners \uc2 SABMiller\uc2  and Molson debating craft acquisitions, \uc2 MillerCoors\uc2  has now done its second deal in less than a year, taking a majority stake in Athens, Ga.-based Terrapin. With TAP set to take full control over \uc2 MillerCoors\uc2  before the end of the year, will more craft beer deals follow? (tripp.mickle@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 19:32 EDT--The administration of Puerto Rico Gov. Alejandro Garcia Padilla late Wednesday fired back at creditors who have been suing the commonwealth over unpaid debts. In a statement, the governor's office called such lawsuits "pointless and counterproductive" and said they strain resources that could otherwise be devoted to debt negotiations. "Creditors suing the Commonwealth will not receive special treatment or secure additional leverage," the statement said. In the most recent suit, filed Wednesday, a group of hedge funds alleged Puerto Rico had violated its three-week old federal restructuring legislation by enacting a moratorium on paying constitutionally guaranteed general obligation bond debt.\par \par \uc2 heather.gillers@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 @hgillers\par \par \uc2 23:18 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/JPY (now at 107.15) will likely remain firm in a 106.50-107.50 range during Asia trade, says Akira Moroga, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  products group at \uc2 Aozora Bank\uc2 . Earlier in the Asia session, stop loss orders brought the USD/JPY to as high as 107.46, its highest since June 7, following media reports the government is considering to put together Y20 trillion ($187 billion) worth economic stimulus later this month. "The biggest theme now is the next week's government stimulus and the BOJ's policy decision," says Moroga. "There may be a sense of accomplishment to cause profit taking. But I think many investors desire to buy on dips," he says, adding that market sentiment remains strong to allow higher USD on solid U.S. data and strong stock market performance. The EUR/USD is tipped in a 1.095-1.105 range qnd is now at 1.1011.\par \par \uc2 (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 19:16 EDT--At \uc2 Campbell Soup Co\uc2 's (CPB) investor day, executives talked about the drastic shift going on in food. "At the heart of it is just the reality of the market now. We have to compete with other big brands, private-label brands, and entrepreneurial brands," said Jeff Dunn, head of CPB's packaged fresh food division. Grocery stores are also struggling to keep up with the changes in consumer preferences. "You can't just waive a wand and add refrigeration to the store," he said, noting that new stores are building in extra fridge space as fresh food overtakes frozen. CEO \uc2 Denise Morrison\uc2  said "we've really been able to really hold our own on shelf space," for soup, despite premium, small-brand soups moving into the aisle. (annie.gasparro@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 23:13 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--As usual, there are no flies on the generic-drug industry. Within hours of a U.S. federal judge refusing to issue a restraining order blocking the market entry of generic versions of the cholesterol drug Crestor, generic firms including Mylan and \uc2 Sun Pharmaceutical Industries\uc2  announced their generic copies were on the way to pharmacies. Crestor maker \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  had requested the restraining order as part of a lawsuit arguing its patent rights should be upheld for all Crestor uses because the company recently won a new approval from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to sell the drug under patent protection for seven more years to treat a rare childhood cholesterol disorder. Crestor had sales of $2.8 billion in the U.S. last year and $5 billion globally. (Jeanne.whalen@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2304 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 Packaging Corp. of America\uc2  (PKG) said 2Q profit rose 2%, with adjusted EPS of $1.25 that topped guidance of $1.18. Sales were $1.42B, compared with Wall Street estimates of $1.46B. Higher volume for corrugated products and reduced energy costs were offset by lower pricing for certain items. But paper price increases led to favorable trends at the end of 2Q and should help 3Q. PKG expects earnings of $1.30 a share, while analysts polled by \uc2 Thomson Reuters\uc2  project $1.27. Shares were flat at $73.78 after hours. PKG, which bought \uc2 Boise Inc\uc2 . in 2013, is on track to close its $386M TimBar Corp. deal in 3Q. (josh.beckerman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 20, 2016 21:00 ET (01:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160721ec7l0003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
