\par\par \b \uc2 USD/SGD Bounces off Downtrend Channel as Yen Falls Further -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2016\par 02:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0034 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/SGD fell overnight, implying a stronger Singapore dollar, as the haven U.S. dollar was sold broadly with a continuation of risk-taking activity sparked by the rally of U.S. stocks to a fresh all-time high. The USD/SGD pair, however, has since bounced off a technical support at 1.3411, the entrance of the Bollinger downtrend channel, delaying the confirmation of a bearish cue. There has been chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from strengthening further, another factor that might be supporting USD/SGD. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  in April set a flat path for the Singapore dollar, as opposed to its previous path of gradual appreciation. Yet, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied to record highs against some of its peers in the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket. Looking ahead, if the yen, which has depreciated 4.6% this week, keeps falling, the Singapore dollar could buckle as well.\par \par \uc2  USD/SGD is now 1.3426 from its Thursday closing of 1.3417. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 14, 2016 20:34 ET (00:34 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160715ec7f00037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
