\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Rises After Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Central-Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2016\par 13:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                       Latest     Change \par  USD/SGD               1.3551  -0.0014 \par  Overnight Rate        0.13%   UNCHANGED \par  2-Year Bond Yield     1.02%    +3 bps \par  10-Year Bond Yield    1.89%    +5 bps \par  2-Year Swap Offer     1.38%    -2 bps \par  10-Year Swap Offer    2.11%    +2 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve  73 bps   +4 bps \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE--The Singapore dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart Tuesday as weakening in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been contained in recent days, possibly by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar traded at S$1.3551 near the close of the Asian trading session, compared with S$1.3565 around the same time Monday.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has risen against the Singapore dollar the past few sessions after the U.K.'s vote to exit from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . The results of the referendum, released Friday, sent shock waves across financial markets globally.\par \par \uc2 Nomura said that it was likely there would be coordinated response among central banks to any global financial-market meltdown, but that at a time of low policy credibility it was unclear how successful such emergency measures would be in an environment of extreme market risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 "For now, financial markets are expected to remain volatile due to the uncertainties that could be unleashed by major changes to the structure of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , and the immediate impact on market confidence and economic behavior," said Lee Sue Ann, \u8206\'20\'0Ean economist at United Overseas Bank.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Singapore 10-year government bonds rose 0.05 percentage point to 1.89%, while that on two-year bonds rose 0.03 percentage point at 1.02%. Yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 Write to Saurabh Chaturvedi at saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 28, 2016 07:48 ET (11:48 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160628ec6s001l7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
