\par\par \b \uc2 Brexit Hangover to Linger on Financial Markets: IG -- Brexit Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 0604 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Financial markets will continue to react for the next couple of weeks to the U.K.'s Brexit vote, \uc2 IG Group\uc2  analyst says. Policymakers will take time to "manage the process in terms of economic policies" in the wake of the U.K. exiting the bloc, Bernard Aw, Market Strategist at London-headquartered financial group tells The Wall Street Journal. He says the U.S. dollar will rise against the Singapore dollar on risk aversion in coming sessions. Reacting to the referendum, the British pound Friday collapsed to its 1985 lows, sending the U.S. dollar rocketing across the board. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are down and among them the Singapore dollar has been most affected, falling nearly 1.0% against the U.S. unit. The U.S. dollar is current trading at S$1.3621 up from Thursday's close of S$1.3368.(saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0604 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] When markets open, the biggest concern will be the implications for the European Union of the U.K.'s vote to leave the bloc, IG analyst Angus Nicholson says. Speculation in the markets will increasingly focus on the weakest links in the \uc2 EU\uc2 , Nicholson says, adding that with Portugal, Italy, Greece, and Spain likely to suffer sharp falls under intense speculation surrounding which nations will be hit most from a hypothetical breakup of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . The pound has suffered the biggest intraday volatility on record, while safe havens like the Japanese yen, gold, and Bitcoin, are up between 4% and 10%, the analyst says. (david.hodari@wsj.com; @davidhodari) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0558 GMT Central banks are likely to enhance the provision of liquidity to the banking system following the U.K.'s decision to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This will likely include reopening of cross-boarder swap lines and stand-by emergency liquidity, according to Chetan Ahya, managing director of Morgan Stanley research. In addition, central banks could likely lean towards a more accomodative policy stance, according to Mr. Ahya. "Initially this would likely be through a change in their forward guidance and only eventually also through a more accommodative policystance." Third, central banks could coordinate their policy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  globally, especially if they were to contemplate potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, says Mr. Ahya. (friedrich.geiger@wsj.com, @FGeiger_WSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0555 GMT "The decision by the people of the United Kingdom in the referendum is a major blow for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," says Michael Menhart, chief economist at reinsurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Munich Re\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "It will have severe implications for the economy -- particularly that of the UK," Mr Menhart says. He now expects a cut in U.K. economic growth by around one percentage point annually through 2018. Economic growth in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  will also suffer, although to a lesser extent, he says. For long-term investors, such as insurers, the decision could mean that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  might hold off near-term rate hikes and thus delay a return to "more normal" interest rates. The decision will likely impact insurers less than other sectors, but London, a big insurance market, will lose standing as a financial center to Singapore or New York, which will affect insurers, Mr. Menhart says. (ulrike.dauer@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0553 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Notices issued by several Chinese banks to their customers ahead of the result of the U.K. referendum, warn of escalating risks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and precious metal markets on Friday due to the vote. The notes say the gap between the rates offered by the banks and market spot rates will likely be wider due to rising volatility and shrinking market liquidity. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . says in its note that it may take steps to limit trading. \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Citic Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . says stop and limit orders, which allow investors to set minimum and maximum prices at which they buy or sell foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , may not be executed at the set prices. Chinese lenders say these measures will be removed once markets stabilize. (grace.zhu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0550 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese reaction so far to a the Brexit vote indicates that authorities erred on the side of optimism. Japan's economy minister Nobuteru Ishihara acknowledges at a news conference that he hadn't expected the U.K. to vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  was forced to hastily convene a news conference because of the yen's jump. Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda is in Switzerland to attend conferences and, at least as of this morning, has no plans to come back to Tokyo, according to a person close to the BOJ. Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  has decided to convene an emergency ministerial meeting later in the day, but the lack of a clear message to send out immediately after the result risks giving the impression they are out of ideas. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0550 GMT Sterling posts steep losses across the board after the U.K.'s unexpected vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Its steepest losses come against the yen as investors dive for safe havens, dropping to a low of 133.29, its weakest level since late 2012, according to Factset data, and is now trading down more than 12% at 138.78. The pound also falls sharply against the euro, although losses are less pronounced due to concerns about the impact for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  as a whole. It trades down around 5.8% at 0.8097 per euro, having hit a low of 0.8320 in highly volatile trade, according to Factset. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0548 GMT The U.K. vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  could have damaging effects on another wealthy European country outside the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Switzerland. "The outcome of the referendum is strongly negative from a Swiss perspective," writes BSI Bank chief economist Stefan Gerlach. The immediate implication for Switzerland is its safe-haven status in times of global unrest which tends to boost demand for franc-based assets. "Safe haven trades will put the Swiss franc under heavy upward pressure and depress Swiss bond yields," says Mr. Gerlach. This will put the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "under intense pressure," he adds. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0545 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Virtual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Bitcoin traded as high as $680.19, driven by investors flight to safe haven assets in the wake of Britain's exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It is now trading up 8.1% at $676.16, according to data from San Francisco-based CoinDesk, a firm which tracks the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The turnaround in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comes after sharp volatility in recent weeks. In the past few trading sessions, Bitcoin's price fell about 25% as the market expected Britain to vote to remain in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while a key Hong Kong-based bitcoin exchange, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bitfinex\f28 \uc2 \f2 , experienced a temporary shutdown because of "networking issues" at its data center. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0541 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia's ringgit has lost 2.7% against the U.S. dollar, as the market reacted to the unexpected U.K. vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The ringgit was earlier Friday weaker by only 0.7% when signs first appeared that the referendum result might be an upset. As the outcome became clearer with more votes trickling in, traders rushed to the U.S. dollar, Japanese yen, and other safe haven assets. Government bond yields fell dramatically, while gold prices rocketed higher. The ringgit is likely to keep sliding, the chart suggests. The USD/MYR will adopt a bullish technical bias if it ends Friday above 4.1260 and inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. But there is hope that the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , joining other Asian central banks that are said to have already stepped in to shore up excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. China, India, and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's central banks have been suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as authorities grapple with the 'Brexit' fallout. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0539 GMT The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could step up its monthly QE purchases to EUR100 billion per month, from EUR80 billion currently, over the coming 1-3 months, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in a research note Friday morning. In reaction to the U.K.'s vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  "could front-load purchases already today -- even without any official announcement. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  could also purchase longer-dated bonds or buy more periphery bonds without announcing changes," the bank says. "We do not expect rate cuts as a tool to limit contagion and \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  also seems less focused on a weaker euro." (todd.buell@wsj.com, @ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0537 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by global central banks and G20 governments may be necessary to stem the selloff arising from a British vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , says Angus Nicholson, a market analyst at IG Markets. However, when there is so much division in Europe at the moment, "it is difficult to see how they can come together and present a unified case that will reassure markets," he says. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 24, 2016 02:04 ET (06:04 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o000lk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
