\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dollar near 1-month high after easing, GDP; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up\b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2015\par 07:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Singapore c.bank reduces rate of appreciation slightly\par     * Singapore dlr up on unwinding bets on bolder easing\par     * Taiwan dollar gains after foreign stock buying\par     * Won up on exporters; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 14 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit a\par near one-month high on Wednesday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  easing was\par seen disappointing to some investors and the city-state's\par economy barely avoided a recession in the third quarter.\par     Regional units rose as the U.S. dollar hovered around\par a 3-1/2-week low against a basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on further\par signs of China's economic slowdown boosted views that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have to wait more for tightening.\par     The Singapore dollar advanced as much as 0.9\par percent to 1.3904 per the greenback, its strongest since Sept.\par 18.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MAS) eased monetary\par policy for the second time this year to support the economy, by\par reducing the rate of appreciation slightly. That defied\par expectations of a bolder step such as such as re-centering of\par its exchange-rate policy band. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manages monetary policy by letting the\par Singapore dollar rise or fall against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its main\par trading partners within an undisclosed trading band based on its\par nominal effective exchange rate (NEER).\par     "The MAS went for the minimal amount of easing required,"\par said Heng Koon How, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par private banking and wealth management in Singapore.\par     The move came as the economy grew 0.1 percent in the third\par quarter from the previous three months on an annualised and\par seasonally adjusted basis. That was better than a 0.1 percent\par contraction tipped in a Reuters poll.\par     Singapore's dollar may gain further in a short term as\par investors may unwind more bets on a bigger easing, but the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to sustain the strength for a longer term\par as the economy is unlikely to regain momentum, analysts and\par traders said.\par     The MAS warned of downside risks to growth due to a slowing\par global economy. Consumer inflation in China cooled more than\par expected in September, while producer prices extended their\par slide to a 43rd straight month, adding to concerns about\par deflationary pressure in the world's second-largest economy.\par  \par     "I would buy USD/SGD around 100-DMA for a return to 1.44 at\par year-end," said Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore, referring to a\par 100-day moving average, currently at 1.3820.\par     \par     ASIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UP\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on broad weakness in the\par U.S. dollar.\par     The Taiwan dollar advanced after foreign investors\par were net buyers in local stock market in the previous\par five consecutive sessions.\par     South Korea's won turned firmer as demand from\par exporters for settlements prompted stop-loss dollar selling.\par     Caution increased over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem the won's strength.\par     Earlier, a South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said the\par won has fallen against the dollar in recent months but not as\par much as other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0525 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.59         119.75       +0.13\par   Sing dlr        1.3947         1.4025       +0.56\par   Taiwan dlr      32.529         32.739       +0.65\par   Korean won     1149.50        1149.70       +0.02\par   Baht             35.57          35.56       -0.03\par   Peso             46.08          46.08        0.00\par  *Rupiah        13614.00       13614.00        0.00\par   Rupee            65.16          65.18       +0.03\par  *Ringgit         4.1815         4.1815        0.00\par   Yuan            6.3464         6.3429       -0.06\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.59         119.66       +0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.3947         1.3260       -4.93\par   Taiwan dlr      32.529         31.718       -2.49\par   Korean won     1149.50        1099.30       -4.