\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Safe-haven bids shine Singapore dollar; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  dips on Chinese stocks slide\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2015\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Foreign banks lift \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dlr to over 2-week high\par     * MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dlr gains\par     * Rupiah hits 17-year low; Aug trade data shows econ woes\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar rose to\par the highest in more than two weeks on safe-haven demand, while\par most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  turned weaker as Chinese stocks\par fell and caution set in ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par interest rate decision.\par     Indonesia's rupiah hit a 17-year low as trade data\par pointed to weak growth in Southeast Asia's largest economy.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar rose as much as 0.6 percent to\par 1.3989 to the U.S. dollar, its strongest since Aug. 28, on\par demand from foreign banks.\par     That came as investors cut bearish bets on emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as some speculated that the Fed would not raise\par interest rates this week due to the recent global market rout\par and fears over a deepening economic slowdown round the world.\par     Among regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , investors sought safer units as\par they waited to see whether the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hike rates\par for the first time in almost a decade at its meeting on\par Wednesday and Thursday.\par     Singapore is seen as a safe-haven in Asia with triple-A\par credit ratings.\par     "It is not surprising that the SGD is relatively stronger at\par 1.40 vs. the USD, given its safe-haven status and relatively\par better economic drivers compared to rest of Asia," said Heng\par Koon How, Credit Suisse Private Bank's senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist.\par     Still, the outlook for the Singapore dollar stayed weak as\par sluggishness in the trade-dependent economy has spurred\par speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may ease monetary policy next\par month.\par     Singaporean banks sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when it was stronger\par than 1.4000 per dollar on rallies on growing caution over\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem its strength,\par especially against the neighbouring Malaysian ringgit \par and rupiah.\par     Against the ringgit, the Singapore dollar rose to a high of\par 3.0771, according to Thomson Reuters data going back to 1990.\par The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also hit a high of 10,267.76 to the\par rupiah, showed Thomson Reuters data going back to 1996.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell 0.3 percent to 14,382 per dollar, its\par weakest since July 1998.\par     Indonesia posted a $430 million trade surplus in August,\par only a third of a revised $1.38 billion surplus in July. That\par was also smaller than the $630 million surplus forecast in a\par Reuters poll.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the\par rupiah's loss as importers bought dollars for payments, traders\par said.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 14,371 rupiah per dollar, its\par weakest since the launch.\par     Jakarta stocks lost 1.2 percent and most government\par bond prices also fell. The 10-year bond yield rose\par to 9.360 percent, its highest since January 2011.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose from its previous close, which\par traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened through usual last-minute\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday.\par     Foreign financial institutions sold the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par stocks fell. Importers also bought the U.S. dollar for\par payments.\par     Traders hesitated to add any positions in the Taiwan dollar\par either way ahead of the Fed's decision, expecting the unit to\par stay around 32.500 per the greenback until then. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0600 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.78         120.24       +0.38\par   Sing dlr        1.4028         1.4075       +0.34\par   Taiwan dlr      32.577         32.720       +0.44\par   Korean won     1185.95        1183.10       -0.24\par   Baht             35.97          36.05       +0.22\par   Peso             46.70          46.74       +0.07\par   Rupiah        14380.00       14345.00       -0.24\par   Rupee            66.42          66.33       -0.14\par   Ringgit     