\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Solid U.S. housing data, Greece caution hurt Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , rupiah exception\b0\par\par\uc2 891 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2015\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah up on bond inflows, short-covering\par     * Won slips; weak yen boosts S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar down, May core inflation at 5-year low\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 23 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slid on Tuesday as solid U.S. housing data powered\par the dollar, while a potential deal to avert a Greek debt default\par was treated with caution. \par     Signs of stabilisation in China's manufacturing sector\par failed to cheer emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the factory\par activity in the world's second-largest economy stayed\par contracting. \par     The Indonesian rupiah bucked regional depreciation,\par hitting a near two-week high, as bond inflows caused investors\par to cut bearish bets on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     South Korea's won fell as a weaker yen \par boosted wariness of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem its outperformance against the\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Singapore dollar weakened as data showed the\par city-state's core inflation in May hit a five-year low.\par  \par     Malaysia's ringgit and Thailand's baht \par eased on a broad strength in the U.S. dollar.\par     The greenback rose against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the euro falling despite hopes for a deal\par to avoid Greece defaulting on upcoming debt repayments. \par     "Greeks merely passed the ball to the Eurogroup. There is no\par deal on the table yet," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par analyst at Maybank in Singapore.\par     "Greece's problems won't be solved so quickly, even though a\par deal will remove some market concerns."\par     U.S. home resales surged to a 5-1/2-year high in May,\par reviving expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could raise\par interest rates as early as September. \par     "We are seeing demand for USD return after it was sold off\par post last week's FOMC. I expect Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken\par against the USD," said Khoon Goh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for ANZ\par in Singapore, referring to the Federal Open Market Committee\par meeting.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  on June 17 signalled that the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par raise interest rates more slowly than markets had expected,\par helping emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rally.\par     "We had good U.S. home sales data overnight, and growth as\par well as policy divergence continues to favour USD versus Asia\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Goh said.\par     \par     WON\par     Caution mounted over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by South Korea's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities as the won on Monday\par strengthened to 8.8985 per yen, its strongest since June 5 when\par the South Korean unit hit a seven-year high versus the yen.\par     The won's strength against the yen has been headache to the\par authorities as South Korean exporters compete against Japanese\par rivals for various products such as cars.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday weakened versus the\par yen.\par     Against the dollar, the won pared some of earlier losses as\par exporters bought it for month-end settlements.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit lost ground as a break of 3.7500 per dollar\par spurred stop-loss selling.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under further pressure as\par investors unloaded it against the neighbouring Singapore dollar\par .\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose as much as 0.4 percent to 13,255 per dollar,\par its strongest since June 11.\par     Custodian banks bought the rupiah from its session low of\par 13,320, traders said. Foreign investors looked to participate in\par the government's bond auction with an indicative target of 12\par trillion rupiah ($904.8 million) later in the day for higher\par yields, they added.\par     Most government bond prices rose, while the rupiah\par strengthened in non-deliverable forwards markets.\par     Traders, however, doubted the sustainability of such bond\par inflows, given a slowdown in Southeast Asia's top economy.\par     "I don't think there is positive market sentiment other than\par yields," said a Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader.\par     "It is still weakening in the long run," the trader said,\par referring to the rupiah.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the worst-performing Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year with a 6.9 percent loss against the\par dollar, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par         \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0555 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.67         123.36       -0.25\par   Sing dlr        1.3387         1.3355       -0.24\par   Taiwan dlr      30.841         30.970       +0.42\par   Korean won     1104.50        1098.80       -0.52\par   Baht             33.72          33.64       -0.23\par   Peso             45.14          45.05       -0.20\par   Rupiah        13290.00       13305.00       +0.11\par   Rupee            63.62          63.51       -0.17\par   Ringgit         3.7460         3.7320       -0.37\par   Yuan            6.2089         6.2095       +0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.67         119.66       -3.25\par   Sing dlr        1.3387         1.3260       -0.95\par   Taiwan dlr      30.841         31.718       +2.84\par   Korean won     1104.50        1099.30       -0.47\par   Baht             33.72          32.90       -2.43\par   Peso             45.14          44.72       -0.93\par   Rupiah        13290.00       12380.00       -6.85\par   Rupee            63.62          63.03       -0.93\par   Ringgit         3.7460         3.4965       -6.66\par   Yuan            6.2089         6.2040       -0.08\par   ($1 = 13,262 rupiah)\par \par  (Additional reporting by Nilufar Rizki in JAKARTA and IFR\par Markets' Catherine Tan; Editing by Eric Meijer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-6-23T07:56:02.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150623eb6n006h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\