\par\par \b \uc2 China Hands out Another Gift to HK Stocks With Fund Scheme -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2015\par 04:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0258 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] A move by regulators to allow Hong Kong asset managers to sell funds in China, and vice versa, is a significant opening, says Citi. The move could accelerate the integration of A/H capital markets, but should deliver a bigger boost to H-shares as China's retail market is 15 times bigger than Hong Kong's. Hong Kong's mutual funds have longer proven track record and should be more a more compelling purchase than mainland mutual funds, it adds. "We believe the direct beneficiaries should be the secondary market asset managers although the extent of benefit could be limited at the initial stage," it says. The indirect beneficiaries include Ping An (2318.HK), Tencent (0700.HK), \uc2 China Resources Land\uc2  (1109.HK), China Southern (1055.HK) and Huaneng Renewable (0958.HK). (joanne.chiu@wsj.com, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @joannechiuhk) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0255 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indonesia's rupiah is nearly unchanged from its Monday close of 12,183, but the daily chart hints at weakness versus the U.S. dollar ahead. The daily USD/IDR Bollinger uptrend channel was activated Monday, setting the dollar on a path higher toward the channel's current ceiling at 12,260. The benchmark U.S. dollar index is notching fresh 1-month highs as the euro slides, providing a catalyst for most USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs Tuesday. USD/IDR will notch a new 17-year high if it surpasses March's peak of 13,245. Greek debt default concerns continue to drag on the euro, thus boosting the U.S. dollar index. If the EUR/USD pair dives below its current technical support level where it now bobs, USD/IDR could easily make new multi-year highs. USD/IDR is now 13,190 from its Monday close of 12,183. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0241 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sunac China\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (1918.HK) deal to take over troubled developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kaisa Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1638.HK) hits another wall. Chinese local media reported that Sunac may be in violation of a Hong Kong stock exchange rule. Which one, exactly, is unclear and difficult to immediately verify, analysts say. If the exchange finds misconduct, Sunac may be forced to pull out of its Kaisa buyout--valued at HK$9.24 billion--and lose the initial payment it made to Kaisa for the potential acquisition, says Chuanyi Zhou, credit analyst for Lucror Analytics. Kaisa and Sunac declined to comment on the allegation, Zhou says in a morning note to clients. Sunac, however, has suspended debt restructuring negotiations because Kaisa's 2014 earnings results remain delayed. A Hong Kong-listed firm can't acquire a target company if it hasn't released recent earnings. Sunac expects to reach an agreement with Kaisa chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kwok Ying-Shing\f28 \uc2 \f2  on how to proceed this week. (Dominique.fong@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0226 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/PHP rallies a second day, again on the back of the overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index, briefly popping into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 44.69. A Tuesday close above this mark would confirm a bullish chart signal that might lead to more peso weakness versus the U.S. dollar in the days ahead. The next chart target would then be the 44.81 ceiling of the uptrend channel. The main driver for dollar strength continues to be the weakening euro, which is a major constituent of the U.S. dollar index. The euro has been weakened due to the possibility of Greek budget restructuring talks failing, which would mean that bailout funds will be withheld and Greece will miss its debt repayments in June. USD/PHP is now 44.67 from its Monday close of 44.62. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0223 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/THB is up slightly, and may activate a bullish chart bias if it ends Tuesday above 33.64 and thereby inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. The benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index continues to creep higher after Monday's rally, thus boosting most USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs. The bearish pressure on EUR/USD due to ongoing Greek debt default concerns has been lifting the dollar index. Fundamentally, USD/THB ought to rise in the medium term because of the dovish rhetoric from the Thai government on interest rates juxtaposed with the likelihood that the U.S. Federal Reserve will raise interest rates this year. Thai authorities have said that a cheaper baht is beneficial for its exporters, and have eased investment outflow restrictions so as to encourage baht weakness. USD/THB is now 33.63 from its Monday close of 33.58. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] OCBC says it continues to expect Singapore's GDP to grow 2.5% this year, compared with an official projection of growth between 2.0% and 4.0%. The government says the economy grew 3.2% on quarter on a seasonally adjusted and annualized basis in the first three months of this year, compared with a preliminary estimate of 1.1% growth released last month. OCBC notes the government lists significant uncertainties to the world economy: China's risk of a sharp correction in its real estate market and uncertainties over Greece's membership to the eurozone. Analysts are divided over when the U.S. Federal Reserve could raise short-term interest rates. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0213 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] CMC Markets thinks the continued strengthening of the USD/SGD on Tuesday despite stronger GDP numbers reported from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "may suggest the influence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." The USD/SGD is at 1.3446, compared with its Monday close of 1.3420. Economists attributed the local dollar's dip on Monday to a bigger-than-expected decline in the consumer price index that might put pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease policy. But on Tuesday morning, the government reported that the economy grew 3.2% on quarter on a seasonally adjusted and annualized basis, compared with a preliminary estimate of 1.1% growth released last month. That should normally support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . CMC says the next resistance level for the USD/SGD could be around 1.3480 while support remains at 1.3400. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0210 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Tocom rubber futures are sharply higher, taking cues from strong gains in Shanghai rubber; the weak Japanese yen also helps. A Singapore-based trader says positive market sentiment now hinges on the return of China demand after the country's recent interest rate cut, and expectations of further stimulus in the short-term. The previous benchmark October Tocom rubber trades Y5.9 higher at Y223.5/kg. The new benchmark November Tocom rubber contract opened at Y220.5/kg and is now at Y225.5/kg. (huileng.tan@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @huileng_tan) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0206 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/MYR now has a bullish technical stance, with Monday's confirmation of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that supports the pair at 3.6070. The buoyancy of the U.S. dollar index - as the euro makes new 1-month lows - is lifting USD/MYR higher Tuesday but the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 3.6340 may limit intraday gains. The growing anxiety that Greece may leave the eurozone has been weighing on the euro. Unless the Eurogroup releases bailout funds soon, Greece won't be able to make debt repayments to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  due in June. If EUR/USD collapses through a key technical support level where it currently rests, the U.S. dollar might spike against the ringgit and other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . USD/MYR is now 3.6200 from its Monday close of 3.6135. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0203 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Singapore dollar weakened versus the greenback after Monday's disappointing inflation data which showed a sixth straight month of deflation, raising the possibility of further policy easing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The weakening of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  affirmed the USD/SGD Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports the pair at a higher level of 1.3376, increasing the odds that the Singapore dollar will keep depreciating. Singapore's economy expanded 2.4% on-year in the first quarter, better than the previous estimate for 2.1% growth, data released Tuesday showed. The Singapore dollar barely reacted to the data. Traders are likely focused instead on EUR/USD, which continues to flounder - thus boosting the U.S. dollar - due to Greek debt default concerns. USD/SGD is now at 1.3447 from its Monday close of 1.3320. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0201 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The recent rally of the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index is keeping USD/KRW propped up inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. If USD/KRW ends Tuesday above 1,094 the bullish chart signal will remain in effect and could keep the South Korea won weak versus the greenback in the near term. However, the pair needs to overcome strong technical resistance at 1,101-1,110 - where the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone caps - before the dollar can rally much higher. Stocks on the benchmark Kospi might get a boost from the improvement in consumer sentiment seen Tuesday; the index rose to 105 in May versus 104 in April. USD/KRW is now 1,098.0 from its Friday close of 1,090.1. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0144 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (020560.SE) moves to improve its safety record are being hindered by a lack of power for its safety czar, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana\f28 \uc2 \f2  pilots and aviation experts say. Safety chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Akiyoshi Yamamura\f28 \uc2 \f2 , brought in after an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana\f28 \uc2 \f2  crash in San Francisco in 2013, doesn't have power over hiring and firing pilots, and can only propose measures that must be approved by a safety panel he doesn't lead. Yamamura "may need to have greater power to raise issues, investigate violations and direct changes," says Tom Haueter, a former U.S. aviation safety officer whom \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana\f28 \uc2 \f2  hired as its representative during the San Francisco crash probe. Yamamura declined to comment. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana\f28 \uc2 \f2  declined to comment on whether his effectiveness is undermined by the company's corporate structure. (Alastair.gale@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 25, 2015 22:58 ET (02:58 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150526eb5q0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
