\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firm dollar, weak China factory activity hurt Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2015\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah down on importers, custodian banks\par     * Won falls on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution; near 7-year high vs yen\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dlr up; March inflation eases less than expected\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 23 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slid on Thursday as the dollar broadly gained on\par solid U.S. data and as disappointing Chinese manufacturing\par activity underscored concerns over a slowdown in the world's\par second-largest economy.\par     Indonesia's rupiah fell on month-end dollar demand\par from importers. South Korea's won eased amid growing\par caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem its strength against\par the yen.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar bucked the trend as inflation\par in March eased less than expected. \par     The U.S. dollar rose versus a basket of six-major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after stronger-than-expected U.S. home sales data.\par  \par     China's factory activity contracted at its fastest pace in a\par year in April, a private survey showed earlier, indicating the\par economy is still deteriorating. \par     "The dismal Chinese manufacturing number and strong U.S.\par housing data may keep weighing on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Yuna\par Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "However, given uncertainties over U.S. rate hikes, those\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely to get out of the recent consolidation."\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell as local importers bought dollars for\par month-end payments and custodian banks joined the bids for the\par greenback.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par lenders to prevent spot rupiah from weakening past 12,950 per\par dollar, traders said.\par     \par     WON\par     The won slid as caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities as it hovered near a seven-year\par high against the yen.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday touched 8.9967 per\par the Japanese unit, its strongest since February 2008.\par     That underscored concerns that South Korea's exporters are\par losing price competitiveness against Japanese rivals.\par     The won pared some of earlier losses as foreign investors\par were set to extended a buying spree in Seoul's main stock market\par  to a 13th consecutive session.\par     Foreigners bought a combined net 3.9 trillion won ($3.6\par billion) worth of equities during the period, the Korea Exchange\par data showed.\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar gained on month-end demand from\par corporates and as leveraged funds bought it.\par     The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a session high of 1.3448 after\par data showing consumer prices in March fell 0.3 percent from a\par year earlier, less than a market expectation of a 0.5 percent\par slide. \par     The data came after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on April 14\par unexpectedly held off from further easing. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0510 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.73         119.92       +0.16\par   Sing dlr        1.3453         1.3479       +0.19\par   Taiwan dlr      31.083         31.113       +0.10\par   Korean won     1082.70        1079.60       -0.29\par   Baht             32.37          32.35       -0.06\par   Peso             44.26          44.23       -0.07\par   Rupiah        12938.00       12895.00       -0.33\par   Rupee            63.05          62.82       -0.36\par   Ringgit         3.6185         3.6115       -0.19\par   Yuan            6.1970         6.1950       -0.03\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.73         119.66       -0.06\par   Sing dlr        1.3453         1.3260       -1.43\par   Taiwan dlr      31.083         31.718       +2.04\par   Korean won     1082.70        1099.30       +1.53\par   Baht             32.37          32.90       +1.64\par   Peso             44.26          44.72       +1.05\par   Rupiah        12938.00       12380.00       -4.31\par   Rupee            63.05          63.03       -0.02\par   Ringgit         3.6185         3.4965       -3.37\par   Yuan            6.1970         6.2040       +0.11\par   \par \par  (Additional reporting by IFR Markets' Catherine Tan; Editing by\par Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-23T06:23:24.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument L