\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Denies 'Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ' to Prop Up Local  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gaurav Raghuvanshi   \par \uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2015\par 11:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday said it hasn't been "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily" to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  said some market commentary had "erroneously" citied the fall in Singapore's foreign reserves and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps since mid-2014 as an indication of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dollar Nominal Effective Exchange Rate. It didn't identify the specific comments to which it was responding.\par \par \uc2 The decline in the U.S. dollar value of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the last nine months till end-March 2015 was due to "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  translation effects" that arose from the broad-based appreciation of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined by US$29 billion to US$249 billion between June last year and end-March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, adding that the decline came after reserves had grown by US$105 billion over the previous five years in U.S. dollar terms.\par \par \uc2 About three-quarters of Singapore's reserves are denominated in the U.S. dollar, euro, British pound and Japanese yen, with no single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocation making up more than one-third of the composition, it said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that it had accumulated a substantial amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, a money-market instrument that it uses to manage liquidity in the banking system, between 2009 and 2011 when there were strong capital inflows to Singapore amid exceptional monetary easing in the major advanced economies.\par \par \uc2 Between June last year and March, the stock of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps fell by US$24 billion to US$34 billion as it allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to mature and increased its reliance on MAS bills as a money-market instrument. Most of the proceeds from the maturing \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps were in excess of what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed in the reserves to maintain confidence in the Singapore dollar, and were transferred to the government for management by GIC Corp. over a longer investment horizon, it said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gaurav Raghuvanshi at gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 14-04-15 0919GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150414eb4e000bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
