\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Dismal China data hurts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Singapore dlr steady before c.bank verdict\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2015\par 08:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit near two-week low vs USD; down vs Singapore dollar\par     * Dividend-linked dollar demand hits won\par     * Rupiah eases on importers; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected\par \par  (Adds desk, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , April 13 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on Monday as disappointing Chinese trade data\par heightened concerns over a slowdown in the world's\par second-largest economy.\par     The Singapore dollar, however, barely moved as\par traders remained wary a day before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy\par statement.\par     Malaysia's ringgit and South Korea's won \par fell to their weakest levels in nearly two weeks. The Indonesian\par rupiah eased as importers bought the dollar.\par     China's exports contracted 15 percent in March from a year\par earlier, defying forecasts for a 12 percent increase. Imports\par also fell 12.7 percent, more than an expected 11.7 percent\par slide. \par     Adding to the sombre mood, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its 2015\par growth forecasts for developing East Asia and China, and warned\par of "significant" risks from global uncertainties including the\par potential impact from a strengthening dollar and higher U.S.\par interest rates. \par     The dollar hovered near its highest since March 18\par against a basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with low yields keeping the\par  euro under pressure.\par     "Weak Chinese data and a solid dollar will hurt Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  further," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst\par at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "Still, their slides may give some short-term opportunities\par to buy on dips. U.S. interest rate hikes are not seen imminent,\par while other central banks may keep pumping money."\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell 1.0 percent to 3.7040 per dollar, its\par weakest since April 1, as interbank speculators and leveraged\par funds sold the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under further pressure from\par selling against the neighbouring Singapore dollar.\par     Five-year government bond yield rose to 3.606\par percent, its highest since March 31.\par     \par     WON\par     The won slid 0.6 percent to 1,098.8 per dollar, its weakest\par since April 2 on dollar demand linked to local companies'\par dividend payments to foreign shareholders.\par     Traders were cautious over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to temper the won's rise as the yen\par stayed weak.\par     Foreign investors were net buyers of both South Korean\par stocks and bonds for a second straight month in March, the\par country's financial regulator data showed earlier.\par  \par     The inflows underpinned the won which hovered close to a\par seven-year high against the yen, adding to concerns\par that a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will erode South Korean exporters'\par competitiveness against Japanese rivals.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah tracked its non-deliverable forwards \par lower.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its losses with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the ailing unit, traders\par said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0520 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.42         120.30       -0.10\par   Sing dlr        1.3689         1.3683       -0.04\par   Taiwan dlr      31.277         31.240       -0.12\par   Korean won     1098.00        1092.70       -0.48\par  *Baht             32.54          32.54       +0.00\par   Peso             44.62          44.55       -0.16\par   Rupiah        12950.00       12910.00       -0.31\par   Rupee            62.38          62.31       -0.10\par   Ringgit         3.7030         3.6670       -0.97\par   Yuan            6.2147         6.2080       -0.11\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.42         119.66       -0.64\par   Sing dlr        1.3689         1.3260       -3.13\par   Taiwan dlr      31.277         31.718       +1.41\par   Korean won     1098.00        1099.30       +0.12\par   Baht             32.54          32.90       +1.11\par   Peso             44.62          44.72       +0.22\par   Rupiah        12950.00       12380.00       -4.40\par   Rupee            62.38          63.03       +1.05\par   Ringgit         3.7030         3.4965       -5.58\par   Yuan            6.2147         6.2040       -0.17\par    * Thailand's financial markets are closed from Monday to\par Wednesday for holidays.\par \par  (Additional reporting by IFR Markets' Catherine Tan; Editing by\par Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-13T07:01:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150413eb4d005l6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
