\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sentiment better as timing of US rate rise less clear\b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2015\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan views optimistic, first time since late January\par     * Singapore dlr short positions fall\par     * Taiwan dollar views positive for first time since October\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 2 (Reuters) - Sentiment towards emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has improved over the past two weeks, with\par views on the Chinese yuan turning optimistic, a Reuters poll\par showed on Thursday, as investors became less convinced U.S.\par interest rates would rise in June.\par     Bearish bets on the Singapore dollar slid, but\par sentiment on the unit was still the third most negative among\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting in\par the city-state later this month.\par     The yuan had long positions for the first time\par since late January, according to the survey of 18 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par analysts and traders from banks and asset management companies\par conducted between Tuesday and Thursday. \par     The bullish bets were estimated to be the largest since\par early December.\par     In March, the yuan rose 1.1 percent against the dollar, the\par largest monthly gain since December 2011, as \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by fixing daily trading mid-points\par higher and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to quell speculation of a further slide.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's bearish bets slid to the lowest since\par late October when it had small long positions at a time of\par improving sentiment on emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Still, the outlook for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains uncertain as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  is set to hold a policy meeting\par in April.\par     A slowing economy and inflation have kept expectations of\par further easing in April alive, even though a poll on March 25\par showed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen maintaining its stance of\par allowing the local dollar to appreciate. \par     Sentiment on the Taiwan dollar became positive for\par the first time since late October. The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par 0.3 percent on foreign inflows and exporters' demand in March,\par when most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell.\par     Long positions in the Indian rupee rose to the\par largest in nearly a month as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  posted its first gain\par in four quarters due to capital inflows.\par     Short positions in the South Korean won fell to a\par near two-month low. Bearish bets on the Indonesian rupiah\par  and the Malaysian ringgit fell to the lowest\par since mid-February.\par     On March 18, the U.S. Federal Reserve dropped a reference to\par being "patient" on rates from its policy statement, opening the\par door wider for an increase this year. But at the same time it\par downgraded its economic growth and inflation forecasts,\par signalling it was in no rush to raise borrowing costs.\par  \par     That prompted investors to shift forecasts of the timing of\par the first rate rise to September from June. U.S. jobs data for\par March due on Friday will provide more clues.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  poll is focused on what analysts believe are\par the current market positions in nine Asian emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht\par .\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars. The figures include\par positions held through non-deliverable forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  2-Apr   -0.13  0.14  0.69  0.74 -0.09 -0.51  1.09  0.13  0.14\par  19-Mar   0.46  1.10  1.48  1.33  0.53 -0.30  1.63  0.33  0.44\par  5-Mar    0.90  0.36  1.24  1.10  0.46 -0.64  1.34 -0.28  0.05\par  18-Feb   0.35  0.32  0.86  0.58  0.39 -0.15  0.74 -0.17 -0.15\par  5-Feb    0.62  0.04  1.16  0.35  0.36 -0.62  1.42 -0.35  0.10\par  22-Jan  -0.04  0.02  0.72  0.38  0.19 -0.73  1.69 -0.02  0.03\par  8-Jan    0.11  0.49  1.05  0.88  0.80 -0.15  1.98  0.13  0.40\par  18-Dec   0.29  0.35  0.89  0.89  0.94 -0.07  1.65 -0.22  0.62\par  4-Dec   -0.51  1.13  1.25  0.43  0.92 -0.47  1.59  0.13  0.47\par  20-Nov  -0.88  1.37  1.12  0.07  0.88 -0.25  1.16  0.50  0.56\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU;\par Editing by Alan Raybould)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-2T08:44:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150402eb42007nd\par }\pa