\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firm yen, higher China PMI give Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  a breather\b0\par\par\uc2 856 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2015\par 07:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won up on offshore funds; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits\par     * Ringgit, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar gain on short-covering\par     * Rupiah rises on inflation data, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , April 1 (Reuters) - South Korea's won led gains\par in emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, tracking a strong\par yen, while an unexpected rise in Chinese factory activity\par slightly eased concerns over a slowdown in the world's\par second-largest economy.\par     Offshore funds bought the won as the yen's\par appreciation weakened worries that South Korean exporters may\par lose competitiveness against Japanese rivals. The Taiwan dollar\par  followed gains in those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with some foreign\par inflows seen.\par     The Malaysian ringgit advanced as investors cut\par bearish bets on the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this\par year. The Singapore dollar rose on short-covering.\par     Indonesia's rupiah gained on slightly higher\par inflation in March. \par     The U.S. dollar broadly eased as the yen \par advanced after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  's tankan survey of business\par sentiment showed that a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to improve\par Japanese corporate sentiment. \par     Adding to further support to emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par China's official Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) edged up to\par 50.1 in March from February's 49.9, defying expectations of a\par slide. \par     Still, traders and analysts doubted how long the reprieve\par from the China PMI would last, especially ahead of U.S. jobs\par data on Friday.\par     The Chinese manufacturing activity also failed to prompt\par optimism over the economy as the index was just barely above the\par 50-threshold, indicating Beijing may have to ease policy\par further.\par     "The main focus for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets this week is Friday's U.S.\par non-farm payrolls number," said Khoon Goh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par for ANZ in Singapore.\par     "While today's better China PMI data has seen Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain, a strong U.S. payrolls number will see the USD\par rally, with Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unwinding the gains seen."\par     Solid U.S. jobs data would add to expectations that the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will hike interest rates this year.\par     In the first quarter, most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell.\par The attractiveness of the region's higher yields was undermined\par by anticipation of higher U.S. interest rates.\par     \par     WON\par     The won rose after South Korea reported a trade surplus of\par $8.4 billion in March, larger than February's $7.7 billion.\par     Caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to prevent the won from strengthening past\par the level of 1,100 to the dollar.\par     Investors also hesitated to chase the won further on \par expectations of a further interest rate cut by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Exports fell the most in two years in March and inflation\par hit its lowest since 1999, weakening economic momentum and\par putting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  under pressure to cut rates again.\par  \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit gained as breaks of 3.7000 per dollar and 3.6900\par spurred stop-loss selling of the greenback.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found further support on higher bond\par prices.\par     The government five-year debt yield fell to 3.585\par percent, while the 10-year bond yield slid to 3.878\par percent.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah advanced as data showed annual inflation in March\par increased to 6.38 percent from 6.29 percent in February.\par     The increase could reduce expectations of an interest rate\par cut.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also spotted buying the rupiah for\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  especially before the data, traders said. \par     Still, local importers bought the greenback on dips for\par payments, limiting the rupiah's upside, traders said.\par     "The 13,000 level is still a good support (for\par dollar/rupiah), unless there is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a\par Jakarta-based trader.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0435 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day   