\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore's key short-term interest rate hits 6-year high\b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * 3-month Sibor rises above 1 pct, highest since Dec 2008\par \par \uc2 * Slower deposit growth vs loans keeps money market tight\par \par \uc2 * Analysts cite possible \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as another factor\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , March 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark three-month interest rate rose above 1 percent for the first time in more than six years on Tuesday, reflecting tighter conditions in the domestic money market and recent weakness in the Singapore dollar.\par \par \uc2 The three-month Singapore interbank offered rate (Sibor), which is used to set floating-rate mortgages, rose to 1.00129 percent, its highest level since December 2008.\par \par \uc2 A softer Singapore dollar can put upward pressure on local interest rates as investors seek higher yields as compensation for holding the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has been bolstered by expectations the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will raise interest rates later this year, while the Singapore dollar has come under pressure after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  (MAS) unexpectedly reduced the upward slope of its policy band in late January.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar fell as low as 1.3938 versus the U.S. dollar earlier this month, the weakest level since July 2010. It has since pulled up from that trough, but is still down roughly 3 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 The MAS manages monetary policy by letting the Singapore dollar rise or fall against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trading partners within an undisclosed trading band based on its nominal effective exchange rate (NEER).\par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar may be another contributory factor, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The rise in Sibor has been driven by tighter domestic liquidity conditions stemming from such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Andy Ji, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Following the inter-meeting surprise, the Singapore dollar NEER slumped to the bottom of its policy band, obliging the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with supplying U.S. dollars. This in turn withdraws \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar liquidity which is not fully sterilised," Ji said.\par \par \uc2 A slower pace of deposit growth relative to loan growth is also keeping money market conditions tight, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 MAS data shows Singapore dollar deposits held by non-bank customers rose 1.1 percent from a year earlier to S$543 billion as of January, while bank loans rose 4.3 percent to S$607.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Incremental deposit growth is much lower than incremental loan growth ... This will keep money markets tight," Kumar Rachapudi, senior rates strategist for ANZ in Singapore, said in a research note. (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano; Editing by Alan Raybould)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-27T10:46:42.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150324eb3o009hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
