\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  losses;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen on  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 916 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah at 17-year low on corp dlr bids, weak stocks, bonds\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spurs short-covering -\par traders\par     * Won hits 20-month trough before c.bank rate decision\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 11 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah hit a\par fresh 17-year low on Wednesday, leading losses among emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to waning risk sentiment, while the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar rose as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupiah fell to a new low, last seen during the\par 1997-98 Asian financial crisis, on dollar demand from local\par companies and as foreign investors sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid lower\par stocks and bond prices.\par     The South Korean won slid to its weakest in 20\par months a day before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's interest rate meeting.\par Malaysia's ringgit touched a six-year low.\par     Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan fell to a\par two-month low and the dollar hit a 12-year peak against the euro\par on views that the U.S. Federal Reserve may raise interest rates\par by mid-year, earlier than expected.\par     That hurt riskier assets both in the United States and\par elsewhere with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P 500\f28 \uc2 \f2  suffering its worst decline in\par two months overnight and emerging market stocks down\par to their lowest since early January.\par     China's industrial output, retail sales and fixed-asset\par investment in the first two months of the year missed market\par expectations, underscoring concerns over a slowdown in the\par world's second-largest economy.\par     "Double whammy of USD strength and risk off tone lifted\par USD/Asia," said Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Sydney.\par     Still, Ji saw some chances of a rebound in emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying the U.S. dollar remains in technically\par overbought territory.\par     He said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's downside was limited\par on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the won may\par head to the 1,100 per dollar level again once \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par stands pat on Thursday.\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar gained as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  looked to support the third worst-performing Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par     On Tuesday, the city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit 1.3910 per dollar,\par its weakest since July 2010. The Singapore dollar has lost 4.4\par percent so far this year.\par     Traders scrambled for the Singapore dollar to cover short\par positions as it strengthened past 1.3880.\par     "Given the MAS' clear determination, the dollar/Sing is\par unlikely to rise as much as others," said a foreign bank trader\par in Singapore, referring to the U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar.\par     Still, many investors sold the city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par rallies due to growing expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par ease policy in April meeting.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell 1.2 percent to 13,240 per dollar, its\par weakest since August 1998.\par     Indonesian government bond prices slid with the 10-year\par yield at 7.568 percent, its highest since Jan. 20.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,164 rupiah per dollar, the\par weakest since the launch.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year, although the\par authorities were not targeting to keep a certain level, traders\par said.\par     On Tuesday, deputy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Perry Warjiyo said\par the authority will always ensure the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was stable\par according to market fundamentals. \par     Indonesia will impose regulations such as temporary\par anti-dumping import duties to help narrow the current account\par deficit and prop up the rupiah, the finance minister said.\par  \par     \par     WON\par     The won lost as much as 0.6 percent to 1,129.6 per dollar,\par its weakest since July 2013 as offshore funds continued to sell\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     South Korea's exporters hesitated to buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for\par settlements amid expectations of further losses, traders said.\par     Investors were awaiting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy\par meeting.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to keep interest rates unchanged\par this week but cut them next month when it revises its forecasts\par to reflect a more tepid economic recovery than initially\par expected, a Reuters poll showed. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0505 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.41         121.14       -0.22\par   Sing dlr        1.3876         1.3905       +0.21\par   Taiwan dlr      31.645         31.566       -0.25\par   Korean won     1127.00        1122.60       -0.39\par   Baht             32.70          32.72       +0.06\par   Peso             44.35          44.27       -0.18\par   Rupiah        13225.00       13088.00       -1.04\par   Rupee            62.82          62.76       -0.10\par   Ringgit         3.7100         3.7035       -0.18\par   Yuan            6.2627         6.2620       -0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.41         119.66       -1.45\par   Sing dlr        1.3876         1.3260       -4.44\par   Taiwan dlr      31.645         31.718       +0.23\par   Korean won     1127.00        1099.30       -2.46\par   Baht             32.70          32.90       +0.61\par   Peso      