\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sliding yen, weak China PMI hit Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Sing dlr up on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2014\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won near 15-month low; exporters limit losses\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted to support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dlr -traders\par     * S.Korea suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check yen/won -traders\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 20 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par fell on Thursday with South Korea's won near a 15-month low as\par the yen lost ground and a private survey of China's\par manufacturing sector increased worries about a slowdown in the\par world's second-largest economy.\par     The Singapore dollar bucked the regional trend as\par traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of supporting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won kept underperforming as it is seen more\par sensitive to the yen's weakness, given the competition between\par South Korea and Japan in exports markets.\par     Indonesia's rupiah fell as investors took profits\par from its gains after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised interest rates and\par the government increased fuel price earlier this week.\par     The yen hit 118.68, a seven-year low against the dollar\par  and a six-year trough versus the euro as\par speculators rushed to carry trades funded by super-cheap\par liquidity from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Asia ex-Japan shares fell after a private survey showed\par growth in China's factory sector stalled in November with output\par contracting for the first time in six months. \par     "Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  became more sensitive to the yen\par after it broke through 115. That indicated a weaker yen is an\par obvious strategy for Japan," said Jeong My-young, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par Futures' research head in Seoul.\par     "Other Asian countries, especially competitors in exports\par markets, are seen following it."\par     \par     WON\par     The won fell 1.0 percent to 1,117.1 per dollar, its weakest\par since Aug. 28, 2013, tracking the yen's weakness.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its losses as\par exporters chased the unit on dips for month-end settlements.\par Some traders covered short positions.\par     Still, investors were looking to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on any\par rallies on growing caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to check its strength against the\par yen.\par     The won advanced to 9.3907 to the Japanese unit, not far\par from a six-year high of 9.3800 hit on Tuesday.\par     Some traders suspected the authorities of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Despite many dollar offers, dollar/won tried to rebound\par whenever it slid. The authorities may have managed," said a\par foreign bank trader in Seoul.\par     South Korea's top officials repeated concerns over the\par impact of the weakening yen on local exporters.\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar rose as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after it fell to 1.3102 to\par the U.S. dollar, its weakest since December 2011.\par     Hedge funds and local companies also bought the city-state's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said as per its estimates the Singapore dollar\par nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) fell below parity for the\par first time since March 2014.\par     NEER-implied U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar thresholds are a\par tad higher currently with parity estimated at 1.3025, it added.\par     "Expect investor caution to prevail in the current vicinity\par with participants looking for any hint of a policy signal,"\par Emmanuel Ng, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with OCBC, said in a\par note to clients.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  maintained its tight\par policy of a "modest and gradual" appreciation of the Singapore\par dollar in October. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manages monetary policy by\par controlling the exchange rate, rather than borrowing costs,\par because trade dominates the economy.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0440 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.46         117.98       -0.41\par   Sing dlr        1.3035         1.3055       +0.15\par   Taiwan dlr      30.905         30.876       -0.09\p