\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Mixed While Greenback Steadies -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 02:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2000-6.2151   6.1800-6.2370 \par USD/TWD   30.500-30.800   30.470-31.000 \par USD/KRW    1,076-1,080     1,070-1,083 \par USD/SGD   1.2653-1.2672   1.2611-1.2700 \par USD/MYR   3.2950-3.3000   3.2800-3.3060 \par USD/THB    32.55-32.62     32.52-32.80 \par USD/PHP    44.90-45.00     44.80-45.20 \par USD/IDR   11,300-11,460   11,120-11,500 \par USD/INR    60.00-60.50     59.50-61.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. Spot USD/CNY may consolidate around the round-figure trading barrier of 6.2000 as the U.S. dollar index was mostly unchanged overnight, suggesting that the PBOC will keep the USD/CNY daily benchmark rate stable. Technical signals on the daily USD/CNY chart indicate bullish momentum will persist as long as the greenback remains above 6.1595 and thus remains in the Bollinger uptrend channel. Chinese stocks appear to have stopped in their tracks as the market is less hopeful now that the authorities will implement direct stimulus measures such as cutting the Reserve Ratio Requirement; some investment banks however think the authorities could increase infrastructure spending for a more targeted effect on growth. In the offshore market, traders are turning less bearish on the yuan, judging by the narrowing price gap between the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract and the 12-month contract. The gap now stands at CNY430 versus CNY565 last week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2000 (round figure trading barrier), then at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1500 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2151 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2370 (12-month high).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD still holds a bullish technical bias, guided by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the pair at 30.470. Persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last said to be around 30.540, has played a part in keeping the Taiwan dollar weak. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could linger near its 2.5-year high of NT$30.667 notched on Monday. The Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep rates steady at its monetary policy meeting today. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.500 (psychological support), then at 30.470 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.370 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.800 (psychological resistance), before 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with upside bias. USD/KRW could resume its bullish path toward 1,083 if it manages to end the day above 1,076 and thereby within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Overnight weakness in the U.S. stock market is casting a shadow on risk-taking in Asia Thursday, thus depressing the South Korea won slightly. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel that opens at 1,076 and could lead the way toward the top of the weekly uptrend channel at 1,083. South Korea on Wednesday revised its 4Q GDP growth lower to 3.7% from an earlier estimate of 3.9%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,076 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), before 1,083 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--likely supported. USD/SGD is currently flirting with technical support between 1.2653-1.2672 which is the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The U.S. dollar needs to break this zone in order to trade lower in the near term. Conversely, if the greenback rises above S$1.2672 by day's ends, there could be a rally ahead for USD/SGD. One factor that might keep a lid on USD/SGD is recent market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buffer the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A couple of traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling USD/SGD near the 1.2780-1.2790 level last week - this will be a psychological barrier that might cap USD/SGD if it gets back up there. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2653 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and entrance to Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2611 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2672 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2718 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consoldation with upside bias. USD/MYR has a bullish technical bias as long as it stays inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 3.2950. However, the resistance at 3.3060, which is the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, may limit gains, hence leading to consolidation for USD/MYR. One trader notes the stability of the ringgit in recent days; a break of the Cloud resistance at 3.3060 could trigger the volatility traders crave. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2950 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2800 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.3060 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3170 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible upside bias. USD/THB may break out higher if it ends the day above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that currently caps at 32.55. A daily close above this mark would also place the greenback in the bullish Bollinger uptrend channel, adding to technical upside bias. Punters are likely leaning toward bets against the baht as the potential for political instability in the near term is high. The ruling by the Constitutional Court that the election held on February 2 was invalid will lead to new elections ahead. This could have repercussions on the Thai economy in the mid-term if violence and protests break out again, affecting tourism, domestic consumption and sentiment for the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.55 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 32.52 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and base of Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.36 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 32.62 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.80 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may hover within a range of 44.90-45.20 after having dropped out of the Bollinger uptrend channel and thus losing its bullish bias. A firm technical base at 44.90 - where the 20-day Bollinger mid line meets the daily Ichimoku Cloud support - will likely keep the dollar firm. Clearer directional cues will emerge if USD/PHP breaks out of this suggested technical range. The greenback has been trading a little weaker as benchmark \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields slipped after reassurance from the U.S. Federal Reserve that interest rates will stay low for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.90 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 44.80 (psychological support), before 44.60 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support and entrance to Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 45.20 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.49 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. The USD/IDR Bollinger downtrend channel remains in effect as long as its 11,460 technical resistance holds. The downtrend channel suggests the next target for the rupiah is 11,120. There has been a respite in rupiah demand this week but steady inflows are likely to continue. Investment bank research shows that mutual funds that left Indonesia last year are now back in the fray again. Investors are focusing on the June presidential elections that will likely boost appeal for Indonesian assets. Historically, Indonesian stocks have mostly rallied in election years. The market is optimistic for presidential candidate Joko Widodo to win - which would be a boon for foreign investor sentiment and could therefore help the rupiah appreciate. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,300 (psychological support), then at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,120 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,460 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,800 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. The Indian rupee could pullback Thursday after a fourth consecutive rally on Wednesday sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an 8-month high of 60.19 and into overbought status on the daily chart. USD/INR now appears overstretched past the lower Bollinger band at 60.50 (standard deviation 2), which implies that a pullback may be seen before the rupee can rally further. The rupee has been rising due to growing appeal of India as an investment destination ahead of upcoming elections commencing next month. Investors are hopeful that a potential change of leadership could herald more business-friendly policies. The Indian rupee has recently outperformed other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to large custodian bank inflows, said a trader. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 59.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.50 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 61.00 (psychological resistance), before 61.15 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 26 Mar 2014 21:02 EDT  USD/Asia Mixed While Greenback Steadies -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 26, 2014 21:02 ET (01:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140327ea3r0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
