\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Subdued but USD/THB Rallies -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 01:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1800-6.2000   6.1500-6.2025 \par USD/TWD   30.500-30.800   30.470-31.000 \par USD/KRW    1,075-1,080     1,070-1,083 \par USD/SGD   1.2672-1.2700   1.2653-1.2718 \par USD/MYR   3.2950-3.3000   3.2800-3.3060 \par USD/THB    32.52-32.56     32.36-32.62 \par USD/PHP    45.00-45.20     44.87-45.48 \par USD/IDR   11,300-11,470   11,140-11,500 \par USD/INR    60.27-60.50     60.00-61.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. Spot USD/CNY may consolidate just under the round-figure trading barrier of 6.2000 as the U.S. dollar index remains subdued, implying that the PBOC will set the USD/CNY daily benchmark rate slightly lower again. The daily chart will remain bullish for USD/CNY in the near term if the greenback remains above 6.1550 and thus keeps the Bollinger uptrend channel intact. Chinese stocks could slide back down as the market is now less hopeful that the authorities will implement stimulus measures in response to the poor China \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash manufacturing PMI for March released on Monday. In the offshore market, traders are less bearish on the yuan, as implied by the narrowing price gap between the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract and the 12-month contract. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1500 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2000 (psychological resistance), then at 6.2025 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2370 (12-month high).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD still holds a bullish technical bias, guided by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 30.470. Persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has played a part in keeping the Taiwan dollar weak. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could linger near its 2.5-year high of 30.667 notched on Monday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.500 (psychological support), then at 30.470 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.370 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.800 (psychological resistance), before 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with upside bias. A slightly softer U.S. dollar index overnight could keep USD/KRW subdued Wednesday. But USD/KRW is still looking bullish on the daily chart, and will remain so as long as it stays above 1,075 by the end of the day. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel supports the dollar at 1,075 and could lead the way toward the top of the weekly uptrend channel at 1,083. South Korea will publish its revised 4Q Gross Domestic Product at 2300 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,075 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), before 1,083 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--supported. USD/SGD is likely to remain firm despite a slightly weaker U.S. dollar index. The daily Ichimoku Cloud support at 1.2672 will likely deter dollar bears. USD/SGD could hence consolidate for now, having lost its bullish technical bias since Monday. The greenback would have to rally and close above 1.2718 in order to reinstate a bullish technical bias. Market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buffer the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days has been keeping a lid on USD/SGD. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2672 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1.2653 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and entrance to Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2718 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2755 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation with upside bias. USD/MYR has a bullish technical bias as long as it stays inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 3.2950. However, the resistance at 3.3060 which is the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone may limit gains, hence leading to consolidation for USD/MYR. Traders may attempt to lean on USD/MYR on the back of a slip in the U.S. dollar index overnight which is casting a slight bearish tone on USD/Asia at the opening. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2950 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2800 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.3060 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3170 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible upside bias. USD/THB may break out higher if it ends the day above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that currently caps at 32.56. The dollar is slightly weaker at Wednesday's opening due to overnight weakness in the U.S. dollar index, but the technical upside bias dictated by the Bollinger uptrend channel could keep USD/THB supported. The ruling by the Constitutional Court that the election held on February 2 was invalid will have repercussions on the Thai economy in the mid-term as tourism and domestic consumption will struggle to recover. Political tension and violence is likely to return--which would also be negative for the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.52 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and base of Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.36 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 32.22 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.56 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 32.62 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.80 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may hover within a range of 44.87-45.20 after having dropped out of the Bollinger uptrend channel and thus losing its bullish bias. A firm technical base at 44.87--where the 20-day Bollinger mid line meets the daily Ichimoku Cloud support--will however keep the dollar buoyant. Clearer directional cues will emerge if USD/PHP breaks out of this suggested technical range. The greenback has been trading a little weaker after reassurance from the U.S. Federal Reserve that interest rates will stay low for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 44.87 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.20 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.48 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR is likely to carry on its bearish path toward 11,140 now that expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates sooner have been dampened. Overnight, the U.S. dollar index remain subdued, leading to early weakness for the dollar in Asia on Wednesday. Now, investors will likely re-focus on the June presidential elections that will likely boost appeal for Indonesian assets. Historically, Indonesian stocks have mostly rallied in election years. The market is optimistic for presidential candidate Joko Widodo to win--which would be a boon for foreign investor sentiment and could therefore help the rupiah to appreciate. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,300 (psychological support), then at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,140 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,470 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,800 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR is likely to trade lower as optimism for a positive change of government at the upcoming elections boosts foreign investor inflows--which has been pushing the rupee higher lately. The rupee hit a 6-month high of 60.43 on Tuesday, making it 2.3% stronger this year. The next technical target for USD/INR may be the base of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support at 60.27. The Indian rupee has recently outperformed other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to large custodian bank inflows, said a trader. The rupee is also benefitting from improving outlook for the country as general elections commence next month. The possibility of a victory for the pro-business BJP opposition party has investors eager to get their foot in the door. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.27 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.50 (psychological resistance), then at 61.00 (psychological resistance), before 61.22 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 25, 2014 20:38 ET (00:38 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140326ea3q00063\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
