\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Retreats on Fed Reassurance -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,895 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 01:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1800-6.2000   6.1500-6.2025 \par USD/TWD   30.500-30.800   30.360-31.000 \par USD/KRW    1,074-1,079     1,070-1,080 \par USD/SGD   1.2700-1.2720   1.2672-1.2756 \par USD/MYR   3.2920-3.3000   3.2800-3.3060 \par USD/THB    32.35-32.48     32.22-32.52 \par USD/PHP    45.00-45.18     44.93-45.48 \par USD/IDR   11,300-11,490   11,160-11,500 \par USD/INR    60.69-61.00     60.50-61.20 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. The overnight weaker U.S. dollar index and the sharp drop in USD/CNY on Monday - which implies the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer actively weakening the yuan - may see the yuan rally again today. Spot USD/CNY could slip toward the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 6.1500 - also a round-figure trading barrier that will support the dollar. The poor China \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash manufacturing PMI for March released on Monday has had little adverse impact on investor sentiment. The consensus view appears to be that the Chinese government might implement stimulus measures to ensure that it can still meet its 2014 economic growth target of 7.5%. The reduced bearishness for the yuan can also be seen in the offshore nondeliverable forward market, where the price gap between the 1-month NDF contract and the 12-month contract has narrowed, implying that traders are less bearish on the yuan's value over a 12-month period. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1500 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2000 (psychological resistance), then at 6.2025 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2370 (12-month high).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--pullback and consolidation. USD/TWD may retreat from its 2.5-year high and head for the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The U.S. dollar fell overnight after \uc2 San Francisco Federal Reserve Bank\uc2  President John Williams said monetary policy remains fundamentally unchanged, reiterating that interest rates won't rise until the second half of 2015. The reassurance from the Fed had a kneejerk effect of weakening the U.S. dollar against the majors, but may also influence USD/Asia lower Tuesday. If USD/TWD stays above 30.460 by the end of the day, the near-term technical upside bias for the greenback may remain in effect. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 30.500 (psychological support), then at 30.460 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.360 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.800 (psychological resistance), before 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation lower. The flushing out of long-USD/KRW positions on Monday may continue Tuesday, fuelled by slightly dovish rhetoric from San Francisco Federal Reserve President John Williams. The Fed official said interest rates won't be raised till H2 2015, which helped to calm skittish investors who have been buying back dollar-shorts since the Fed's policy meeting last Wednesday. USD/KRW could retreat toward the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1,074 and then consolidate. However, if this support is upheld by the end of the day, the near-term bias for the U.S. dollar is still bullish. Weakness at the opening of the South Korea stock market could keep won strength at bay. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 1,074 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,071 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1,070 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,079 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,080 (psychological resistance), before 1,083 (7-week high).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation lower. USD/SGD may consolidate lower toward the daily Ichimoku Cloud support at 1.2672 now that it has lost its bullish technical bias after having fallen out of the Bollinger uptrend channel that had been supporting at 1.2720. Reassurances from the U.S. Federal Reserve that interest rates will not be raised until the second half of 2015 took a toll on the U.S. dollar overnight. Coupled with market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days to buffer the Singapore dollar, USD/SGD topside is likely to be very limited for now. If USD/SGD drops under the Ichimoku Cloud - which bottoms out at 1.2647 - it would also be within the Bollinger downtrend channel that could pull the U.S. dollar even lower in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support at 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2672 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1.2647 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and entrance to Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2720 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2756 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation lower. USD/MYR could retreat lower toward the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.2920. The dollar is softer Tuesday after reassurance from U.S. Federal Reserve official John Williams that U.S. interest rates will stay low until the second half of 2015. The dollar is also well-capped by technical resistance that has failed to break on two attempts, implying that it is less likely to rise for now - this could motivate traders to take profit on long-dollar positions and thus weigh on USD/MYR. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 3.2920 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2800 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.3060 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3170 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB is likely to bob within a range of 32.35-32.48 demarcated by the Bollinger mid-line support and the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. Despite weakness in the U.S. dollar overnight - triggered by mildly dovish rhetoric from the U.S. Federal Reserve - USD/THB remained stable due to underlying anxiety that the domestic political situation could worsen. Thailand investors may be slightly anxious after the Constitutional Court on Friday ruled that the election held on February 2 was invalid. Political tension and violence is likely to return - which would be negative for the Thailand economy and thereby for the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 32.35 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 32.22 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.10 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.48 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.52 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 32.56 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation lower. USD/PHP has dropped out of the Bollinger uptrend channel and may slip to the Ichimoku Cloud support at 44.93 next. The U.S. dollar is trading on the weak side Tuesday after San Francisco Federal Reserve President John Williams said that U.S. interest rates will not be raised until the second half of 2105. The reassurance may depress the dollar in Asia and thereby help the peso to recover losses sustained after the Fed appeared hawkish at its policy meeting last week. Traders said that medium-term investors are now turning bullish on the U.S. dollar and may look for opportunities to buy on dips. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 44.93 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 44.88 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.18 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.48 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR is likely to carry on its bearish path toward 11,160 now that expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates sooner have been dampened. Overnight, the U.S. dollar index subsided after San Francisco Federal Reserve President John Williams reassured markets that U.S. interest rates will not be raised until the second half of 2105. Now, investors will likely re-focus on the June presidential elections that will likely boost appeal for Indonesian assets. Historically, Indonesian stocks have mostly rallied in election years. The market is optimistic for presidential candidate Joko Widodo to win - which would be a boon for foreign-investor sentiment and could therefore help the rupiah to appreciate. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR at 11,300 (psychological support), then at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,160 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,490 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 24 Mar 2014 20:52 EDT  USD/Asia Retreats on Fed Reassurance -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR could keep trading lower as foreign investor inflows propel the rupee toward more strength. The underlying bullishness for the U.S. dollar due to expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve might turn more hawkish has been dampened. On Monday, San Francisco Federal Reserve President John Williams reassured markets that U.S. interest rates willl not be raised until the second half of 2105. The rupee could hit a 6-month high if it surpasses 60.60 notched on March 11. The next technical target for USD/INR may be the base of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support at 60.27. The Indian rupee has recently outperformed other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to large custodian bank inflows, said a trader. The rupee is also benefiting from an improving outlook for the country as general elections commence next month. The possibility of a victory for the pro-business BJP opposition party has investors eager to get their foot in the door. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 60.69 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 60.50 (psychological support), before 60.27 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.00 (psychological resistance), then at 61.20 (psychological resistance), before 61.27 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 24, 2014 20:52 ET (00:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140325ea3p0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
