\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Retreats but May Stay Bullish Mid-Term -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 01:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2200-6.2300   6.2000-6.2500 \par USD/TWD   30.500-30.800   30.450-31.000 \par USD/KRW    1,079-1,080     1,074-1,090 \par USD/SGD   1.2750-1.2800   1.2720-1.2831 \par USD/MYR   3.3000-3.3060   3.2910-3.3170 \par USD/THB    32.22-32.50     32.20-32.52 \par USD/PHP    45.17-45.47     45.06-45.50 \par USD/IDR   11,300-11,500   11,245-11,800 \par USD/INR    60.74-61.00     60.50-61.20 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The yuan may regain some ground this week after steep losses last week sent spot USD/CNY into overbought territory on the daily chart. A pullback may hence occur before further USD/CNY strength can take place. The market will be awaiting the March HSBC China Flash Manufacturing PMI report due at 0145 GMT for clues as to whether the economy is indeed slowing as fast as some analysts think. A strong number could help reassure investors that February's weak data was indeed due to the extended Lunar New Year holiday. In the USD/CNY nondeliverable forward market, the gap between the benchmark 1-month contract and the 12-month contract remains wide--a hint that offshore investors are bearish on the yuan, expecting it to be depreciate within a year; this contradicts analysts' expectations released early this year for 1.0%-1.5% appreciation. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2200 (psychological support), then at 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.1972 (daily upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2). Immediate resistance is at 6.2300 (psychological resistance), then at 6.2370 (12-month high), before 6.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--upside bias. USD/TWD has taken on a bullish bias now that it has entered the Bollinger uptrend channel. However, the mildly weaker U.S. dollar index could delay immediate gains for USD/TWD. As long as the greenback stays above 30.450 by the end of Monday, the technical uptrend channel remains in play and could lead the dollar to 31.000 in the near term. Investors have turned more bullish on the greenback after the U.S. Federal Reserve was more hawkish than expected at its policy meeting last week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.500 (psychological support), then at 30.450 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.340 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.800 (psychological resistance), before 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--possible pullback lower. USD/KRW may retreat from the technical resistance at the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and pullback toward the base of the channel at 1,074. However, if this support is maintained by the end of the day, the near-term bias for the U.S. dollar is still bullish. The U.S. dollar was mildly softer on Friday, but the consensus underlying view that the U.S. Federal Reserve will keep up its hawkish tone will likely support the greenback on any dips. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,079 (upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 1,074 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (psychological resistance), before 1,090 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. USD/SGD retains its bullish technical bias as long as it stays inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 1.2720. The sudden drop in USD/SGD late Friday prompted market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under assault last week due to the change in investor sentiment towards the U.S. dollar after the unexpectedly hawkish stance of the U.S. Federal Reserve. USD/SGD could keep rising toward the weekly technical resistance at 1.2831 as long as the daily Bollinger uptrend channel remains in play. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2750 (psychological support), then at 1.2739 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2720 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2831 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--pullback lower. USD/MYR could retreat lower now that it has met strong technical resistance at 3.3060 where the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud meets the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Coupled with a slightly weaker U.S. dollar index, there is increased likelihood for USD/MYR to drift lower toward 3.2910. There is, however, likely to be underlying support for the greenback as the medium-term investors have now turned bullish on the U.S. dollar on the back of the hawkish U.S. Federal Reserve. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.2910 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3060 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3170 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB is likely to bob between a range of 32.22-32.50 demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1). The U.S. dollar may drift slightly lower within this band on cue from the drop in the U.S. dollar index overnight. The daily and weekly technical charts both paint a murky picture for USD/THB. Unless the dollar breaks this 32.22-32.50 range, the market may meander for a while longer. Thailand investors may be slightly anxious after Thailand's Constitutional Court on Friday ruled that the election held on February 2 was invalid. Political tension and violence is likely to return--which would be negative for the Thailand economy and thereby for the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.22 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.20 (psychological support), before 32.09 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.50 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.52 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 32.58 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. USD/PHP may keep climbing this week if it manages to stay above 45.17 Monday. The technical support at 45.17 is the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that could lead the U.S. dollar higher toward 45.47 in the near term. The greenback may have edged lower on Friday, which could drag USD/PHP lower, but the strong buying by macro hedge funds reveals that medium-term investors are now bullish on the U.S. dollar and will likely remain so for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.17 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.06 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.47 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.50 (psychological resistance), before 45.80 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation lower. Technical resistance at 11,500 coupled with mild weakness in the U.S. dollar index could see USD/IDR drift lower toward psychological support at 11,300. As long as the barrier at 11,500 is not broken by the end of the day, there is still a bearish bias for USD/IDR in the near term. The market has been covering U.S. dollar shorts after the unexpectedly hawkish tone of the U.S. Federal Reserve last week. But as the June presidential elections draw nearer, there could be renewed optimism for presidential candidate Joko Widodo to win--which would be a boon for foreign investor sentiment and could therefore help the rupiah to appreciate again. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,300 (psychological support), then at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,180 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,500 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation lower. USD/INR is likely to drift lower toward the 60.80 base of the Bollinger downtrend channel. The Indian rupee has recently outperformed other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to large custodian bank inflows, said a trader. These inflows are helping to depress USD/INR, keeping it away from the technical resistance level on the daily chart at 61.30. The rupee inflows may taper off this week but the bearish USD/INR technical bias could keep the rupee strong. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.74 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 60.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.00 (psychological resistance), then at 61.20 (psychological resistance), before 61.60 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 23, 2014 20:41 ET (00:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140324ea3o0003e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
