\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dollar, ringgit tad higher on short-covering\b0\par\par\uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2013\par 03:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Leveraged funds buy Singapore dollar     * Malaysian bond yields lower     * Won gives up early gains on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution   (Adds text, updates prices)     By Jongwoo Cheon     \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar and the Malaysian ringgit edged up on Tuesday as investors further reduced bearish bets on weakened views that the Federal Reserve may start scaling back its stimulus, while most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely changed.     The Indian rupee weakened to within touch of a record low, pressuring bonds, although caution over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited its downside.       The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar advanced on demand from leveraged funds. The ringgit gained as Malaysian government bond yields fell.     The U.S. dollar slid further as data showed on Friday that U.S. employers slowed the pace of hiring in July, raising expectations that the Fed may wait until late this year before reducing its bond-buying programme.\par \par \uc2          "If the dollar continues to lose traction globally, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue to reclaim lost ground, given also that the net portfolio inflow environment has continued to improve in recent sessions," \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  said in a client note.     Still, emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains were limited as some traders stayed cautious over the Fed's possible tapering and on weaker regional stocks.     Dallas Fed President \uc2 Richard Fisher\uc2  said on Monday the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nearer to dialing back its quantitative easing after the unemployment rate dropped last month.      Investors were awaiting the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy decision later in the day. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  is considered almost certain to cut rates a quarter point to 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     Leveraged funds lifted the Singapore dollar, but investors\par hesitated to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher than 1.2640 to the U.S.\par dollar, traders said.\par     Based on the charts and technical factors, traders said the\par greenback will find a trendline support around the level.\par     "Everybody is looking to buy the U.S. dollar there," said a\par foreign bank trader in Singapore.\par     For more gains in the Singapore dollar, it needs to\par strengthen past the 1.2630-1.2640 level first and clearly breach\par 1.2600, the trader said.\par     "But nobody expects that for the time being," he added.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit edged up in thin trading as 10-, five- and\par three-year bond yields   slid.\par     But foreign funds were waiting to buy dollars around 3.2200,\par limiting the ringgit's upside, traders said.\par     "Since last week's NFP, timing of U.S. tapering is in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 doubt," said a senior Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur,\par referring to the July U.S. nonfarm payrolls, which were weaker\par than market expectations.\par     The ringgit is seen still having room to strengthen to\par 3.2100, but it needs to clear 3.2200, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     WON\par     The won earlier gained on exporters' demand for settlements\par and stop-loss dollar selling.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, turned slightly lower on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities. Traders also stayed wary of the Fed's potential\par policy shift.\par     "The won is unlikely to break the 1,110 level soon. We still\par have uncertainties over the U.S.," said a senior foreign bank\par trader in Seoul.\par     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   Change on the day at 0350 GMT\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        98.00          98.28       +0.29\par   Sing dlr        1.2664         1.2688       +0.19\par   Taiwan dlr      29.946         29.950       +0.01\par   Korean won     1114.55        1113.80       -0.07\par   Baht             31.37          31.33       -0.13\par   Peso             43.52          43.47       -0.11\par  *Rupiah        10280.00       10280.00       +0.00\par   Rupee            61.11          60.88       -0.38\par   Ringgit         3.2280         3.2315       +0.11\par   Yuan            6.1234         6.1247       +0.02\par  \par   Change so far in 2013\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        98.00          86.79      -11.44\par   Sing dlr        1.2664         1.2219       -3.51\par   Taiwan dlr      29.946         29.136       -2.70\par   Korean won     1114.55        1070.60       -3.94\par   Baht             31.37          30.61       -2.42\par   Peso             43.52          41.05       -5.68\par   Rupiah        10280.00        9630.00       -6.32\par   Rupee            61.11          54.99      -10.01\par   Ringgit         3.2280         3.0580       -5.27\par   Yuan  