\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2013\par 03:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \par USD/CNY   6.1350-6.1419   6.1283-6.1487 \par USD/TWD   29.890-29.930   29.750-30.000 \par USD/KRW   1,114-1,120     1,110-1,122 \par USD/SGD   1.2606-1.2672   1.2530-1.2700 \par USD/MYR   3.1680-3.1800   3.1560-3.1920 \par USD/THB   30.80- 31.00    30.67-31.17 \par USD/PHP   43.00-43.44     42.80-43.58 \par USD/IDR   10,100-10,200   10,000-10,300 \par USD/INR   59.50-60.00     59.00-60.03 \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- downside bias. The dollar index slides overnight after another round of poor data from the U.S., raising the possibility of a stronger yuan benchmark rate to the dollar Wednesday. Comments on Tuesday from Chinese Premier Li Keqiang about a 7.0% 'floor' for economic growth have reverberated globally, underpinning improving risk appetite. The yuan is hence likely to be on firmer ground, and the USD/CNY could thus rally toward the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 6.1283. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for the USD/CNY is at 6.1350 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1283 (Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1419 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.1487 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.1500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD --consolidation. The USD/TWD is likely to rest upon the Ichimoku Cloud support at 29.890 unless the USD/CNY parity rate comes in sharply lower, which could send USD/TWD down toward the Cloud's base at 29.750 via proxy effect. On a daily close below 29.750, more downside becomes more likely for the dollar. China's Premier adopting an informal 'floor' on the country's economic growth rate is likely to bolster confidence for Asia and could therefore benefit Asian stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.890 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 29.750 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.930 (top of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological resistance), before 30.060 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- consolidation, possible downside bias. The USD/KRW is still caught inside the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone and may thus consolidate for now. But if the base of the Cloud at 1,114 is breached at the end of the day, more downside for the dollar will likely follow. Factors for a downside move include a weaker USD index following another round of weaker U.S. economic data released overnight, as well as the retreat of USD/JPY further away from 100.00. The South Korean won tends to trade with a positive correlation with the Japanese yen. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,114 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1,110 (psychological support), before 1,109 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,120 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological resistance), then at 1,122 (top of Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1,130 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- consolidation. The USD/SGD may hover within a 1.2606-1.2700 range demarcated by the entrance to the Bollinger downtrend channel and the psychological barrier above. A weaker USD index may have limited impact on the USD/SGD pair as the latter approaches key support ahead of 1.2600 where the Bollinger channel and the Ichimoku Cloud roughly coincide. Tame inflation data and a lowered official inflation outlook released Tuesday also reduces the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the SGD strong via market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said one domestic dealer, who is turning slightly bearish on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2606 (Bollinger downtrend channel and Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1.2600 (psychological support), before 1.2530 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2672 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2700 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- downside bias. The USD/MYR borders on the entrance of the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 3.1680. A stronger downside bias could emerge if the pair ends the day below this key support level. The next target for a deeper downside move would be the 3.1500 psychological barrier. The greenback trades lower overnight on another round of weak U.S. data, casting further doubt on expectations that the Federal Reserve will taper quantitative easing this year. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support lies at 3.1680 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1560 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.1500 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.1800 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 3.1920 (Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2000 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- downside bias. The USD/THB slides as the greenback once again comes under pressure due to weaker U.S. economic data released Tuesday. The USD/THB may next target psychological support at 30.80 as expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to trim its pace of asset purchases will likely fade even more. The weekly Ichimoku Cloud support zone comes in around 30.79, and this could prop up the dollar and thereby cap further baht gains this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.80 (psychological support), before 30.67 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 31.00 (psychological barrier), then at 31.17 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.20 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation lower. The USD/PHP may get a push lower due to the U.S dollar index sliding overnight on weaker U.S. economic data, which reduces the likelihood of the Federal Reserve tapering QE3 this year. The USD/PHP pair could drop toward the 43.00 psychological mark but seems unlikely to break this barrier due to persistent buying of the dollar on dips. The dollar may thus trade in a 43.00-43.44 range, capped by the 200-week moving average resistance line. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.00 (major psychological support), then at 42.80 (psychological support), before 42.72 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 43.44 (200-week moving average), then at 43.50 (psychological resistance), before 43.58 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation with upside bias. The rupiah is likely to stay on a weakening trend as the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has apparently stepped away from supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, allowing the USD/IDR pair to spike as high as 10,250 -- a level not seen since July 2009 -- from its prior closing of 10,060. The change in attitude of \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  is likely to encourage more traders to bet that the rupiah will decline. Indonesia's Finance Minister said in an interview with Wall Street Journal published Monday that the rupiah is depreciating in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- possibly a hint that the government wants to boost exports by making them relatively cheaper. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for the spot USD/IDR is at 10,100 (psychological support), then at 10,000 (major psychological support), before 9,990 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 10,200 (psychological resistance), then at 10,300 (psychological resistance), before 10,550 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation. The USD/INR could slip lower as the greenback softens generally due to another round of weaker U.S. economic data released overnight. Any further rupee strength will likely come as a result of dollar weakness rather than optimism for the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupee barely reacted to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's latest move Tuesday to rein in access to rupee funding -- an attempt to force banks to buy more rupees in the spot market and thereby strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  on Monday also announced new restrictions on gold imports, a move that could help reduce the country's huge current account deficit which exists partly due to India's strong appetite for gold. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.50 (psychological support), then at 59.00 (psychological barrier), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 60.00 (major psychological resistance), before 60.03 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 23, 2013 21:05 ET (01:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130724e97o000ig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
