\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah at 4-year low; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to see weekly losses\b0\par\par\uc2 1,147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2013\par 03:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Corporate dollar demand hits rupiah; c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2      * Rupiah to see largest weekly decline in 13 months     * Won higher on exporters, short-covering   (Adds text, updates prices)     By Jongwoo Cheon     SINGAPORE, July 19 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit a near four-year low on Friday, leading declines among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the day and the week as the region may see more capital outflows on expectations of the Federal Reserve's reduction in stimulus.     The rupiah stayed under pressure from dollar demand from local companies, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit its downside.     The Malaysian ringgit and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar  also fell in thin trading as investors covered short positions in the greenback before the weekend.     The South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar  bucked regional declines, helped by local exporters.     But the North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not free of worries from the more dismal outlook on overall emerging \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders and analysts said.     Japan's appetite for foreign assets grew with the country's investors net buyers of foreign bonds for a second straight week last week by purchasing the largest amount since September 2012.       Still, it is premature to expect inflows of the money to emerging Asian assets, analysts said.     "It looks difficult for the Japanese to increase their Asia allocation given weak growth momentum and the Fed," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures research head in Seoul.     "In the very, very long term, we may see Japanese money going to other parts of Asia. But it is too early to expect it now," Jeong added.     Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  said on Wednesday the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still expects to start scaling back its monthly bond-buying of $85 billion a month later this year although he left open the option of changing that plan if the economic outlook shifted.     Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are on course to post weekly declines, led by the rupiah.     The rupiah's indicative price fell 0.9 percent against the dollar so far this week, according to Thomson Reuters data. If the loss is maintained, that would be the largest weekly fall since the period ended June 1, 2012.     The Indian rupee has also lost 0.4 percent so far this week, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government took steps to stabilise the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .     The rupiah and rupee \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen more vulnerable to capital outflows on the Fed's policy shift due to worries about their current account deficits.     During the last two weeks, short positions in the two units increased with bearish bets on the rupiah at the highest level since November 2008, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.       For the week, the ringgit has declined 0.8 percent to the dollar, while the Singapore dollar has fallen 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah's indicative prices lost as much as 0.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to 10,100 per dollar, the weakest since September 2009 on\par corporate dollar demand. Foreign banks also bought the\par greenback.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded weaker than the prices in\par thin liquidity with some banks bidding dollars above 10,400,\par traders said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted providing dollars and some\par exporters joined the selling, but they were not seen enough to\par satisfy dollar demand, they added.\par     "Definitely, if BI doesn't supply enough dollars," a trader\par said when asked if the rupiah is expected to weaken further.\par     "Dollar supply is limited. There is no interbank market.\par Where can we get dollar supply if it is not from BI?"\par     On Thursday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it raised $600 million in\par its first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps auction, well above its indicative\par target of $500 million, in an effort to increase ammunition for\par the defence of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar edged weaker as a break of 1.2690 to\par the greenback prompted some stop-loss selling in thin liquidity,\par traders said.    \par     Still, the city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut much of its initial\par slide as it has a chart support at 1.2714, the 50 percent\par Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation in July.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit eased on caution over bond outflows and as\par investors covered short dollar positions before the weekend.\par     Earlier weakness in the Singapore dollar also weighed on the\par Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     "People were back to buying USD with some custodian outflows\par on MYR bonds and better U.S. sentiment," said a foreign bank\par trader in Singapore.\par     But the ringgit recovered most of its initial losses as it\par found a trendline support around 3.0250 per dollar, another\par trader in Kuala Lumpur said.      \par     \par     WON\par     The won rose on demand from local exporters for settlements\par and as investors covered short positions before the weekend.\par     Earlier, the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on dollar bids from\par importers for payments.\par     But the local unit turned higher on expectations that it\par would find more support from month-end corporate demand, traders\par said.\par     "Exporters' support may be stronger next week as the\par month-end is approaching," said a senior foreign bank trader in\par Seoul.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose in thin trade from Thursday's close.\par Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had pushed it lower through\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the prior session.\par     Taiwanese exporters showed interest in buying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par when it was weaker than 30.000, traders said.\par     But foreign financial institutions and domestic importers\par bought U.S. dollars on dips, limiting the Taiwan dollar's\par upside.\par     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par   Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       100.13         100.43       +0.30\par   Sing dlr        1.2675         1.2660       -0.12\par   Taiwan dlr      29.926         30.025       +0.33\par   Korean won     1122.90        1126.30       +0.30\par   Baht             31.11          31.07       -0.13\par   Peso             43.38          43.43       +0.13\par   Rupiah        10085.00       10055.00       -0.30\par   Rupee          