\par\par \b \uc2 jongwooEM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strong GDP growth spurs demand for won; record yuan powers Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 969 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2013\par 03:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * S.Korea exporters support won, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr at 6-wk high on exporters, foreign investors\par \par \uc2 * Yuan proxy trades lift ringgit, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar\par \par \uc2 * Baht down on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , finmin comments, weak bonds\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 25 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose on Thursday after the country reported better-than-expected growth in the first quarter while a record- high yuan helped drive regional units seen as proxy plays higher.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also supported by expectations that central banks in the world's biggest economies will continue to keep or even expand monetary stimulus after disappointing economic data from the United States and Germany.\par \par \uc2 "Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have room to appreciate a little more on expectations of more monetary policy expansions by Japan and Europe," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures' research head in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 Stronger momentum for the yuan which hit its highest against the dollar led to greater demand for the Malaysian ringgit and the Singapore dollar as a proxy trade.\par \par \uc2 Still, it is hard to see further gains in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the yen stayed weak, traders and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The yen's weakness resulting from \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's bold monetary easing is seen hurting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of export rivals such as South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Some countries such as Philippines have taken measures on concerns over hot money inflows.\par \par \uc2 "It as been tough for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise as the yen sunk. There are also fears of capital controls," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thio Chin Loo in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting the views, the Thai baht fell and the Philippine peso's gains were limited.\par \par \uc2 Philippine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced the rate on a peso short-term deposit scheme that is popular with both foreigners and local investors and used by the authorities to manage domestic market liquidity, as expected.\par \par \uc2 But it left its benchmark interest rate on hold at a record low.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won gained as offshore funds bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Asia's fourth-largest economy grew in the first quarter at its fastest pace in two years despite the yen's weakness.\par \par \uc2 Exporters joined the bids for month-end settlements and bond inflows also supported the won, traders said.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders added, as the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 hit its strongest since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 Investors maintained the dark outlook for the economy as both consumers and exporters struggle for confidence.\par \par \uc2 "It became more difficult to expect the won's weakness. But I doubt further stock gains and some investors appeared to hold dollar short positions. So, I don't think the won can appreciate further," said a foreign bank trader in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 "Most of all, the authorities will do something, given the yen/won level," the trader added.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar rose 0.5 percent to 29.672 per U.S. dollar, its strongest since March 14 as exporters' demand for settlement intensified with the month-end coming.\par \par \uc2 Foreign financial institutions also bought the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit rose as investors bought it to bet on a stronger yuan and on demand linked to daily fixing, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Some interbank traders cut long positions in the dollar to stop losses as the greenback were hit by weak U.S. durable goods orders for March.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors hesitated to add more bullish positions in the ringgit on sustained caution over the upcoming election on May 5.\par \par \uc2 "Good dollar buyers will come out at 3.0300 which is still 100 pips away. People still want to short the ringgit ahead of the election," said a foreign bank trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar gained on the yuan proxy trading and as the city-state's stocks rose.\par \par \uc2 Investors are awaiting March factory output, which rose a seasonally adjusted 8.1 percent from the previous month, according to Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht slid as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on weaker bonds, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year Thai government bond yield rose to 3.47 percent from Wednesday's 3.36 percent, while the five-year yield advanced to 3.03 percent from 3.01 percent.\par \par \uc2 Inflows to the country's bonds were a major driver of the baht's appreciation.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0750 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currenc