\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar down as pace of January inflation slows\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2013\par 06:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar fell slightly on Monday after the city-state reported a slower-than-expected inflation rate in January.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 0.2 percent to 1.2393 to the U.S. dollar as at 0529 GMT after consumer prices in January rose 3.6 percent from a year earlier, below a forecast of a 4.0 percent rise.\par \par \uc2 Before the data, the Singapore dollar stood at 1.2391.\par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar may weaken more if the yen falls further and the euro drops," said a senior Asian bank trader.\par \par \uc2 "It is possible to see 1.2410. But no more than that," said the trader, noting that other emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven't fallen much on the day.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar has a 200-day moving average at 1.2408. Once that level is broken again, it may weaken to 1.2465, the 38.2 percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation between June and October, according to analysts.\par \par \uc2 On Feb 21, it closed weaker than the average for the first time since June.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Monday, it hit 1.2407 to the U.S. dollar and threatened to go past the average.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, stronger-than-expected growth data helped the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoy a 0.4 percent gain against the greenback, its largest daily percentage appreciation since Jan. 10, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar has lost 1.4 percent against the U.S. dollar so far this year on worries about a slowing local economy and caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130225e92p00079\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
