\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2013\par 01:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par            Immediate Range   Larger Range \par  \par    USD/CNY 6.2123-6.2203     6.2000-6.2283 \par    USD/TWD 29.225-29.280     29.170-29.500 \par    USD/KRW  1,080-1,088       1,073-1,090 \par    USD/SGD 1.2340-1.2400     1.2300-1.2473 \par    USD/MYR       -                 - \par    USD/THB  29.76-30.00       29.62-30.08 \par    USD/PHP  40.52-40.72       40.50-40.92 \par    USD/IDR  9,700-9,800       9,620-9,900 \par    USD/INR  53.61-53.86       53.50-54.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation with upside bias. A broad strengthening of the greenback is likely to send the PBOC central parity rate higher again today, possibly above 6.2850. Spot USD/CNY might thus trade with an upside bias. The pair could rise above the Bollinger downtrend channel, which now caps at 6.2203, and head to the 20-day Bollinger mid at 6.2283. A close above the Bollinger mid could add bullish technical momentum to USD/CNY. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 6.2203 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2283 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.2364 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.2123 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2100 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (major psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- upside bias. USD/TWD is likely to rally after Friday's breakout from the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 29.225. Short-covering, triggered by the pair's spike Friday, is likely to be the next driver. Late last week, oil importers were said to be buying large amounts of USD, which might have started the run, says an NDF dealer. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 29.280 (Nov. 11 high), then at 29.500 (psychological resistance). Initial support is at 29.225 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 29.170 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 29.120 (20-day Bollinger mid and base of Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- upside bias. USD/KRW is experiencing a deep short-squeeze that is worrying even the mid-term short-USD positions, with the pair rising past the 1,080 psychological mark. Fear of a North Korea nuclear test disrupting investor sentiment is the main reason behind the won's sudden decline over the last few sessions. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 1,088 (20-week Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,090 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 1,080 (psychological support and base of Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1,073 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), before 1,068 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- upside bias. USD/SGD is biased higher as the U.S. dollar powers higher across the board, except against the EUR. USD/SGD could soon hit the 1.2400 psychological mark, which might stall the pair in the near term. The Singapore dollar is at its weakest since October 2012, but has moved in tandem with other Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the yen, so it is unlikely to worry \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thus MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not expected to cap USD/SGD's rally, unless it spikes violently. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 1.2400 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2473 (monthly Bollinger mid). Immediate support is at 1.2340 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 1.2300 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2265 (20-day Bollinger mid support).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- closed for Thaipusam holiday.\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- upside bias. USD/THB may be about to challenge the psychological resistance at 30.00 soon, given the broad-based strength of the USD. As the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as MYR and SGD also decline against the dollar, so too the baht is expected to fall. A break of the 30.00 psychological watermark could trigger a deluge of short-covering in USD/THB and possibly send the pair past the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.08; this would add to bullish bias. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.00 (psychological resistance), then at 30.08 (ceiling of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.41 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance). Immediate support is at 29.76 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.62 (Jan. 21 low), before 29.50 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- upside bias. USD/PHP could bust out of the Bollinger downtrend channel, which currently caps at 40.72, as the greenback rallies across the board. Exit from the downtrend channel suggests the USD/PHP downtrend is over and a reversion to the Bollinger mid at 40.92 is possible. A break of the 20-day Bollinger mid could spook short-term speculators into buying back their shorts. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 40.72 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.92 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 41.00 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 40.52 (bottom of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.50 (psychological support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 40.25 (5-year low).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- upside bias. USD/IDR is likely to rally back above the 9,800 psychological mark in the grey market as traders anticipate another dollar shortage situation onshore. The recent rally in the USD index is triggering widespread buying of the greenback in Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. This is likely to trigger short-covering in USD/IDR, specifically in the grey market which had been trying to short the dollar towards the end of last week as signs of normalizing in the spot market appeared. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance), then at 9,9000 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 9,700 (psychological support), then at 9,620 (official spot level), before 9,600 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- short-term upside bias. The dollar is expected to rise against the Indian rupee, following similar gains in other Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. USD/INR could test the top of the Bollinger downtrend channel at 54.12, but first the psychological resistance at 54.00 may provide keen resistance. The mid-term bias for USD/INR is still lower, as long as the pair stays under the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone which currently hovers at 54.28. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 53.86 (weekly Bollinger mid resistance), then at 54.00 (psychological resistance), before 54.12 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate support is at 53.61 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 53.50 (psychological support), before 53.00 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 28-01-13 0057GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130128e91s0000x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
