\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -US fiscal deal powers Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Korea,  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  spotted  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,063 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2013\par 02:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won at 16-mth high on offshore funds, exporters\par \par \uc2 * S.Korea studying ways to curb "one-way bets" on won\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by S.Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted - dealers\par \par \uc2 * Ringgit hits 2-1/2-mth high vs dlr on catch-up plays\par \par \uc2 * Philippine peso up on remittances; U.S. names chase baht\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 2 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  started 2013 on a firmer note on Wednesday, fuelled by stronger appetite for riskier assets after a last-minute U.S. fiscal deal to avoid a recession in the world's top economy.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won hit a 16-month high against the dollar on demand from offshore funds and exporters, although the country warned against further sharp appreciation with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit jumped on catch-up plays and carry trades, while U.S. investors powered the Thai baht . The Philippine peso also gained on remittance inflows.\par \par \uc2 U.S. lawmakers earlier approved a deal preventing huge tax hikes and spending cuts that could have pushed the Asia's major export market off the "fiscal cliff" into recession.\par \par \uc2 The agreement pushed up Asian stocks to a five-month high, dampening the yen to its lowest level since July 2011.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to stay firm, although regional authorities will keep slowing down their appreciation, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "News that the fiscal cliff has been avoided is a clear positive for risk appetite. As such, it should be good news for Asia ex-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while weighing on the yen," said Callum Henderson, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research with Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "With the global outlook remaining uncertain to some extent, Asia ex-Japan central banks are stepping up their efforts to limit or delay local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation for now," he added.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said the country is studying policy options to deal with a possible rise in one-way bets on the won. Another ministry official also warned of action against speculation.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying U.S. dollars through agent banks, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 With such steps by regional authorities, some of emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the won may suffer from short-term corrections, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 But a bullish trend in regional units will stay intact as long as investors seek higher-yields amid easier monetary policies of major central banks, they added.\par \par \uc2 "There could be some profit-taking in a near term. But that won't last, as the fundamentals argue for further strength in Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Frances Cheung, senior strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won hit 1,063.2 per dollar, its strongest since Sept. 2, 2011, on demand from offshore funds and domestic exporters.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean unit also touched 12.1701 to the yen, its firmest since May 2010.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted slowing down the won's gains, in addition to official warnings, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "It is up to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the won can strengthen further or not," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit touched 3.0330 per dollar, its strongest since Oct. 18, as local investors and offshore funds built up bullish bets on last month's underperformer among regional units.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed 0.6 percent against the dollar in December due to bids for the greenback from domestic corporates, becoming the second-worst performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Indian rupee, Thomson Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit also hit 2.4838 to the Singapore dollar , its firmest since Oct. 26 on carry trades, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar edged up, but its upside was limited as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted especially after hitting 1.2201 to the greenback, dealers said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors barely reacted to data showing the city-state's economy grew more vigorously than foreseen in the fourth quarter of 2012, avoiding an expected recession.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso advanced to 40.87 to the greenback, its strongest since Dec. 6 on remittance inflows and as local interbank speculators added fresh long positions.\par \par \uc2 But caution also grew over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with short-term forwards negative, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Further gains are possible, but I am not sure if it can break 40.85 today with onshore swap points in the negative," said a foreign bank dealer in Manila, referring to the peso's session high on Dec. 5.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 U.S. investors pushed up the baht, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The baht is seen staying firm on inflows and demand from real money names, but investors stayed wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0635 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        87.26          86.72       -0.62\par  Sing dlr        1.2205         1.2219       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      29.006         29.136       +0.45\par  Korean won     1063.30        1070.60       +0.69\par  Baht             30.45          30.61       +0.53\par  Peso             40.89          41.05       +0.40\par  Rupiah         9670.00        9630.00       -0.41\par  Rupee            54.38          54.68       +0.56\par  Ringgit         3.0375         3.0580       +0.67\par *Yuan            6.2303         6.2303       -0.00\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        87.26          86.79       -0.54\par  Sing dlr        1.2205         1.2219       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      29.006         29.136       +0.45\par  Korean won     1063.30        1070.60       +0.69\par  Baht             30.45          30.61       +0.53\par  Peso             40.89          41.05       +0.40\par  Rupiah         9670.00        9630.00       -0.41\par  Rupee            54.38          54