strong support just above S$1.2400 Monday. Several banks estimate that the $1.24 level is consistent with the upper end of the Singapore dollar NEER, suggesting MAS would likely come in at that level to tamp down the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 "It's always at the back of your mind that they might come in," said an analyst at a local bank.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were unchanged, holding up well even amid heightened buying of equities Monday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Martin Vaughan at martin.vaughan@dowjones.com [ 06-08-12 0812GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120806e886000my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
