\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: MAS Needn't Worry About SGD Move Lower - Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2011\par 08:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0712 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] While other Asian central banks have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be keeping its powder dry and has no reason to be concerned with the level of the SGD for the time being, says a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank. "There is still a two-way flow on the Singapore dollar," the dealer says, adding that some corporate selling has capped USD gains against the local unit. The USD/SGD has gained steadily by a total of just over 2% in the last week; it is now around 1.3103 in very choppy trade. (martin.vaughan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 15-12-11 0712GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1026 1085 1851 5012 5038 55110 55114 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111215e7cf000d4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or